INSERT INTO memories VALUES(1,'global',NULL,replace('MCP tool availability is PERSONA-SCOPED (OpenWorker, as of 2026-08-20): a persona''s manifest `mcp:` list decides which of the 12 gateway servers it gets; `mcp: [none]` means none. Current profiles: research -> arxiv, tavily, context7, exa. repo-ops -> github, filesystem, qdrant, arxiv. fastchat -> none (the full 12-server surface costs ~16k prompt tokens and 90s of prompt processing per turn on the local 27B model). IMPORTANT HISTORY: before 2026-08-20 scheduled automations had NO MCP tools at all — `prepare_mcp_tools` was only called from the WebSocket handler, so a scheduled run naming `arxiv-search_papers` or `qdrant-qdrant-store` was calling tools it could not see and silently fell back to shell/curl. That is now wired into `_run_scheduled_task`. If a tool call fails with ''unknown tool'', check the persona''s `mcp:` list first — the server is probably just not in this profile. GATEWAY CREDENTIAL STATE: as of 2026-08-24 the gateway''s github server token is BROKEN — `github-list_commits` returns `MCP error -32603: Authentication Failed: Bad credentials`, reverting the 9 private iconbaypark2900 repos to 404 for the repo-activity automation (last verified working 2026-08-20). Until the token is refreshed, repo-activity brief coverage is effectively 1/10 (only liaison-agentSystem).\n\nAGPACK test suite: as of 2026-08-28 the full pytest suite is GREEN (203 passed) — was 10 failed / 72 passed on import (before `git add pyyaml`). Fixes made this run: (1) trust/audit.py validate() now names the offending field + kind in its error (added `_detail_bad` helper); (2) trust/delegation.py Scope gate: removed a redundant isinstance step so the real "closed set" scope check fires (a bare string scope is refused); (3) several delegation test-setup bugs (hop signature/ownership, chain root-tail/cycle, CapabilityPolicy.scopes frozenset API); (4) artifact/validator.py had a latent NameError — it referenced `pydantic.ValidationError` without importing `pydantic` (fixed by adding `import pydantic`); (5) `pyyaml` was a missing dependency, now installed. Reproduced output kept in .scratch/reproduce_full.txt (the .scratch dir is a private copy under the workspace).','\n',char(10)),'agpack full pytest suite GREEN (203 passed) as of 2026-08-28; trust suites fixed, validator.py pydantic import added',NULL,NULL,'2026-08-16 17:53:33');
INSERT INTO memories VALUES(2,'workspace',NULL,'9 of the 10 repos in the iconbaypark2900 "Repo activity brief" automation (dcode-stack, workstation-stack, ragtradesystem, sigma, qgg_research, materialScience, setup, polymarket_btc, sourcelab_ai_production_scaffold) are PRIVATE; only liaison-agentSystem is public. No GITHUB_TOKEN/GH_TOKEN or gh auth exists in the OpenWorker shell, so those 9 always 404 and cannot be reported on. Fix = set a token in env. Discovered 2026-08-19.','9 of 10 activity-brief repos are private, unauth''d GitHub access is all we have','/home/iconbaypark2900/OpenWorker/__task__task-717e4360ea',NULL,'2026-08-20 20:37:03');
INSERT INTO memories VALUES(3,'workspace',NULL,'The grant/funding digest workspace (resume.txt for Jonathan Beale) already contains grants-2026-week-33.md from a prior run (verified 2026-08-20). This digest is a scheduled weekly job; prior digests accumulate as grants-YYYY-week-WW.md. New digests should reference/update rather than duplicate prior weeks'' findings, and closed programs already covered can be briefly carried forward.','Digest runs accumulate weekly files; week-33 digest already existed','/home/iconbaypark2900/OpenWorker/__task__task-092a6d85f2',NULL,'2026-08-20 21:13:01');
INSERT INTO memories VALUES(4,'workspace',NULL,'AGPACK test suite: as of 2026-08-28 the full pytest suite is GREEN (203 passed). MANIFEST FIXED on 2026-08-28: [project.dependencies] in pyproject.toml previously declared only cryptography>=42 (validator.py worked only because pydantic/pyyaml happened to be installed — a fresh `pip install .` would silently drop them and break verify()). Corrected to pydantic>=2, cryptography>=42, PyYAML>=6. Rationale: validator.py imports pydantic + yaml (module-level, artifact/validator.py:35 and artifact/packager.py:59); schema.py imports pydantic (artifact/schema.py:54); PyYAML is used by validator._check_within_max_cap. wasmtime / opentelemetry-api / typer are intentionally NOT declared — nothing in the source imports them yet. Deps verified with tomllib. Verified: `python -m pytest -q` from repo root = 203 passed. (Earlier 08-28 fixes that made it green: trust/audit validate() names offending field+kind; delegation Scope closed-set gate; validator pydantic import added; pyyaml installed.)','AGPACK now declares pydantic/cryptography/PyYAML in pyproject deps; 203 tests pass','/home/iconbaypark2900/OpenWorker/__task__task-717e4360ea',NULL,'2026-08-20 21:53:47');
INSERT INTO memories VALUES(5,'global',NULL,replace('Qdrant (localhost:6333) — KB used collection `default`, named vector `fast-all-minilm-l6-v2`, 384-dim Cosine, stored via the local fastembed path (ingest_kb.py-style HTTP PUT/points + POST/points/query, dedup threshold 0.72) because the MCP qdrant tools are persona-scoped (the KB-ingest run''s persona did not carry them). Point IDs: use str(uuid4) — bare string IDs 400. PAYLOAD KEY THE READERS USE IS "document" (NOT the qdrant-store tool''s "information"): using "information" as the raw payload key is what broke qdrant-find.\nSTATE CHANGE 2026-08-27: `default` collection was DELETED (was 58 points as of 08-26) and does not exist; only `fdot_surplus_documents` exists (0 points, vectorless = cannot embed/search). Recreated `default` to keep the KB usable. fastembed was also missing; installed it — default model now BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5 (384-dim, compatible size). Since `default` is freshly created and empty, dedup on 2026-08-27 ran against a fresh collection; all 08-27 findings were cross-checked against the 08-26 ledger''s stored subjects to rule out real dups.','\n',char(10)),'Qdrant KB `default` deleted 2026-08-27, recreated; fastembed now installed (bge-small 384-dim)',NULL,NULL,'2026-08-20 23:48:20');
INSERT INTO memories VALUES(6,'global',NULL,'User stated (2026-08-20): wants to build an open-source, Claude-Science-class stack combining OpenEvolve (AlphaEvolve-style evolutionary coding agent, GitHub algorithmicsuperintelligence/openevolve) with quantum chemistry for drug discovery + materials science. Components in play: OpenEvolve as optimization loop, open structure models (Boltz-2/Chai-1/ESMFold), RFdiffusion+ProteinMPNN design, PySCF/Psi4/ML-potential scoring, RDKit. Explicit goal: match Anthropic''s Claude Science polish — unified workflow over fragmented tools, auditable artifacts/provenance, flexible compute. Treat OpenEvolve/QM/drug-discovery questions as this ongoing project, not one-off help.','Building open Claude-Science-class OpenEvolve+QM stack for drug discovery and materials',NULL,NULL,'2026-08-21 01:27:45');
INSERT INTO memories VALUES(7,'workspace',NULL,'mwb DEPLOY (session 2026-08-28): The broker now has a real VPS deploy package under packages/gateway/ — `src/server.ts` (Node stdlib http, no Express; routes GET /, GET /health, POST /fetch, GET /audit, GET /audit/dashboard; 100% env-driven: PORT/RAIL_ID/RAIL_PRICE_MICROS/PER_CALL_CEILING_MICROS/ORIGIN_URL [unset=self-origin]/IDENTITY_KEY_ID/IDENTITY_SUBJECT). Runs TS SOURCE via tsx at runtime (no compiled dist/). Deployment gotchas learned through debugging: (1) Dockerfile MUST `COPY packages ./packages` BEFORE `npm ci` — otherwise the @mwb/* workspace symlinks in node_modules are never created. (2) Do NOT set NODE_ENV=production in the Dockerfile — that makes `npm ci` omit devDependencies, which drops tsx. (3) WORKDIR is /app/packages/gateway and CMD is `npx tsx src/server.ts`. (4) Running `npm start` at the WORKSPACE ROOT resolves to the ROOT package.json (no start script) — it only works from packages/gateway/, which defines `"start":"tsx src/server.ts"`. (5) Image CMD is `npx tsx ...` (NOT `npm start`); fix stale docs accordingly. makeFetchId emits only digits (alphabet is 10 digits; it indexes `Math.floor(rand()*16) % 10`). CI (ci.yml) runs: npm ci, npm run typecheck, npm test, npm run conformance <fixture> <name>.','mbar gateway VPS deploy via tsx source-run; Dockerfile gotchas (packages-before-npm ci, no NODE_ENV=prod, WORKDIR gateway)','/home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace',NULL,'2026-08-23 19:58:24');
