INSERT INTO sessions VALUES('__run__run-a23d84f180','/home/iconbaypark2900/OpenWorker/__task__task-0db7112de6','ollama:qwen3.8-27b:latest','interactive','⏰ Scheduled run — Weekly research corpus -> Qdrant','repo-ops',187,NULL,'[]',0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,'2026-08-20 23:51:12','{"tools": ["grep", "list_files", "read_file", "read_file_lines", "remember", "run_shell", "todo_write", "web_fetch", "web_search", "write_file"], "commands": []}','{"boundary_index": 98, "summary_text": "**Primary request and intent**\n\nScheduled weekly automation (do NOT create/modify scheduled tasks). Build this week''s research corpus from arXiv and store it in local Qdrant (collection `default`) so the user''s agents can retrieve it later.\n\nStanding constraints:\n- Search 4 topics SEPARATELY (quantum computing, materials science, ML systems, agents) \u2014 never merge into one query.\n- Must read the actual abstract before judging relevance; never judge from title alone.\n- Only store what was actually read (no fabrication).\n- Dedupe: check Qdrant before storing; skip duplicates.\n- Budget: \u2264 4 arXiv searches, \u2264 20 abstract reads, \u2264 15 stored papers.\n- Every entry must carry a real arXiv ID from tool output.\n- If a topic returns nothing, say so and move on; do not fill from memory.\n- Write a summary file `corpus-<YYYY-MM-DD>.md` grouped by topic with arXiv IDs.\n- Do not send without approval (implicit: this is an automation producing a local artifact, no external send step defined).\n\n**Key concepts and decisions**\n\n- Qdrant 1.19.0 running at `http://localhost:6333`, collection `default`, single vector named `fast-all-minilm-l6-v2` (384-dim, Cosine distance, MiniLM via `fastembed`).\n- Payload schema: `{\"document\": \"<str>\", \"metadata\": {\"topic\": \"...\", \"arxiv_id\": \"...\", \"date\": \"YYYY-MM-DD\", \"source\": \"arxiv-weekly\"}}`.\n- Qdrant 1.19.0 uses the **legacy insert shape**: `{\"ids\": [\"uuid\"], \"vectors\": [[...384 floats...]], \"payloads\": [{...}]}` \u2014 NOT the newer `{\"points\": [...]}` shape.\n- Delete endpoint uses `{\"points\": [\"uuid\"]}` (not `{\"ids\": [...]}`).\n- The `ids` field MUST be a JSON array of UUID strings (a bare string fails).\n- Embedding: `fastembed` library confirmed available; produces numpy arrays that must be converted to Python lists before JSON serialization.\n- arXiv API: `http://export.arxiv.org/api/query` with `search_query`, `sortBy=submittedDate`, `sortOrder=descending`, `max_results=40`, date-range filter for last 7 days.\n- 15 papers selected across 4 topics (quantum=4, materials=4, mlsystems=3, agents=4 \u2014 approximate split; exact list is in `store_corpus.py`).\n- Abstracts: 19 total reads (16 first batch + 3 re-reads), within the 20 budget.\n\n**Artifacts and files**\n\n| File | Role | State |\n|------|------|-------|\n| `store_corpus.py` | Main script: embeds 15 paper descriptions with fastembed, dedupes via scroll, inserts into Qdrant. Contains the full list of 15 papers (topic, arxiv_id, title, one-sentence finding). | Edited multiple times: URL paths fixed to include `/collections/`, ndarray\u2192list fix, insert body switched to legacy `ids/vectors/payloads` shape. Currently ~119 lines. |\n| `dump_existing.py` | Utility to scroll existing points in Qdrant for dedupe check. | Working; confirmed 1 pre-existing point (Vulkan/ROCm note). |\n| `search_arxiv.py` | Runs 4 topic searches on arXiv API (last 7 days, newest first), prints results. | Working. |\n| `fetch_abstracts.py` | Fetches abstracts by ID list (first batch of 16). | Working. |\n| `fetch_abstracts2.py` | Re-fetches 3 abstracts (2608.15609, 2608.13756, 2608.17275) that scrolled off. | Working. |\n| `q1.xml`\u2013`q4.xml` | Cached arXiv search XML from a prior run. | Present but stale; fresh searches done via `search_arxiv.py`. |\n| `probe.json` | Temporary test payload for Qdrant insert debugging. | Discrepancy. |\n| `corpus-2026-08-20.md` | **NOT YET CREATED** \u2014 the final deliverable summary. | Pending. |\n\nWorkspace root: `/home/iconbaypark2900/OpenWorker/__task__task-0db7112de6/`\n\n**Errors and fixes**\n\n1. **Missing `/collections/` in URL path**: `store_corpus.py` had `f\"{QDRANT}/{COLL}/points/scroll\"` but Qdrant requires `f\"{QDRANT}/collections/{COLL}/points/scroll\"`. Fixed via replace_in_file; verified with `grep -n \"QDRANT}/\"`.\n\n2. **Mangled constants line**: A bulk replace accidentally removed the `=` and string values from line 11 (`QDRANT, COLL, VECTOR_NAME = \"http://localhost:6333\", \"default\", \"fast-all-minilm-l6-v2\"`). Fixed via targeted replace_in_file.\n\n3. **ndarray not JSON-serializable**: `v` from fastembed was a numpy array. Fixed by `[float(x) for x in v]` (or `list(v)`).\n\n4. **Wrong insert API shape (400 error)**: Qdrant 1.19.0 does not accept `{\"points\": [{\"id\",\"vector\",\"payload\"}]}`. Must use `{\"ids\": [\"uuid-string\"], \"vectors\": [[...]], \"payloads\": [{...}]}`. Fixed the body construction in `store_corpus.py`.\n\n5. **`ids` as string vs array**: `{\"ids\": \"test-probe\"}` \u2192 400. Must be `{\"ids\": [\"uuid\"]}`. Discovered via iterative probing.\n\n6. **Delete API shape**: `{\"ids\": [...]}` \u2192 400. Correct shape is `{\"points\": [\"uuid\"]}`.\n\n7. **Points inserted but not visible in scroll**: After a \"successful\" insert (response `status: ok`), scrolling the collection still shows only 1 point (the original). Reproduced with single-point inserts using `wait:true`. This is an **UNRESOLVED** issue at the point the conversation ends. Qdrant 1.19.0 is confirmed on port 6333 (bound to 127.0.0.1).\n\n**All user messages**\n\n1. *(Scheduled run trigger)*: Full task specification \u2014 build 4-topic arXiv corpus (last 7 days), read abstracts, dedupe, store \u226415 in Qdrant with specific payload schema, write `corpus-<date>.md`. Budget: 4 searches, 20 reads, 15 stores. Rules: only store what you read, use real arXiv IDs, don''t fill gaps from memory, don''t create/modify scheduled tasks.\n\n(No other user messages in this turn; the rest is assistant autonomous execution of the scheduled task.)\n\n**Pending tasks**\n\n- **Resolve the Qdrant insert-persistence issue**: Points are reported as inserted (`status: ok`) but do not appear in subsequent scroll. Need to determine whether this is a `wait` flag issue, a version-specific quirk, a write-ahead-log delay, or a proxy/middleware layer on port 6333 that acknowledges but discards writes. The last probe (`e1d5e7b8-0000-4000-a000-000000000042`) was inserted with `wait:True`; the assistant was about to read it back.\n- **Successfully store all 15 papers** into Qdrant collection `default`.\n- **Write `corpus-2026-08-20.md`**: summary grouped by topic with arXiv IDs, listing what was stored (or noting empty topics).\n- **Update todo list** to reflect completion.\n\n**Current work**\n\nThe assistant is debugging why Qdrant 1.19.0 at `localhost:6333` accepts point inserts (returns `{\"status\":\"ok\"}`) but the points never appear in `scroll`. The last concrete action was:\n\n- Inserted probe `e1d5e7b8-0000-4000-a000-000000000042` with `wait:True` via a Python script writing `probe.json` then `curl -d @probe.json`.\n- Was about to `sleep` and re-scroll to confirm whether this single point persists.\n- Also checked `curl -s http://localhost:6333` \u2192 confirmed Qdrant 1.19.0, and `ss -ltnp` \u2192 listener bound to `127.0.0.1:6333`.\n\nThe `store_corpus.py` script is functionally complete (correct URL paths, correct legacy insert shape, correct vector conversion) **except** the insert silently fails to persist. The response-parsing bug (trying to read `resp[\"result\"][\"operation_info\"][\"statuses\"]`) crashes the script after the HTTP call succeeds, but the underlying issue is that the data never appears.\n\n**Next step**\n\nInvestigate why inserts are not persisting in Qdrant 1.19.0. Concrete next actions:\n1. After the last probe insert, scroll again and also try `GET /collections/default/points/e1d5e7b8-0000-4000-a000-000000000042` to check if the point exists but scroll is filtering it.\n2. Check Qdrant''s optimizer status and whether `wait:true` is actually being honoured (the legacy API may ignore it).\n3. Try a `PUT` or check if the collection has `write_timeout` or is in a degraded state (`curl -s http://localhost:6333/collections/default` \u2192 look at `status`, `indexed_vectors_count`, `points_count`).\n4. If it''s a version quirk, consider whether a different endpoint or a `wal` flush is needed, or whether the process serving 6333 is a thin proxy that drops writes.\n5. Once a successful, verifiable insert is achieved, re-run `store_corpus.py` (fix the response-parsing to handle the legacy success shape `{\"result\":{\"status\":\"indexed\"}}` or similar) and confirm all 15 points are visible.\n6. Write `corpus-2026-08-20.md` with the 15 papers grouped by topic.", "working_state": "## Working state (extracted mechanically from tool records)\nFiles written/edited (most recent first):\n- store_corpus.py\n- fetch_abstracts2.py\n- fetch_abstracts.py\n- search_arxiv.py\n- dump_existing.py\nRecent shell commands:\n- python3 -c \" import json body={''ids'':''test-probe'',''vectors'':[[0.1]*384],''payloads'':[{''document'':''probe'',''metadata'':{''topic'':''t'',''arxiv_id'':''0000.00000'',''date'':''  [ok]\n- python3 -c \" import json body={''ids'':[''e1d5e7b8-0000-4000-a000-000000000001''],''vectors'':[[0.1]*384],''payloads'':[{''document'':''probe'',''metadata'':{''topic'':''t'',''arx  [ok]\n- curl -s -X POST http://localhost:6333/collections/default/points/delete -H ''Content-Type: application/json'' -d ''{\"ids\":[\"e1d5e7b8-0000-4000-a000-000000000001\"]}  [ok]\n- curl -s -X POST http://localhost:6333/collections/default/points/delete -H ''Content-Type: application/json'' -d ''{\"points\":[\"e1d5e7b8-0000-4000-a000-000000000001  [ok]\n- python3 store_corpus.py 2>&1 | grep -v \"it/s\\]\\|Fetching\"  [ok]\n- curl -s -X POST http://localhost:6333/collections/default/points/scroll -H ''Content-Type: application/json'' -d ''{\"limit\":200,\"with_payload\":true}'' | python3 -c   [ok]\n- sleep 5; curl -s -X POST http://localhost:6333/collections/default/points/scroll -H ''Content-Type: application/json'' -d ''{\"limit\":200,\"with_payload\":true}'' | py  [ok]\n- python3 -c \" import json, urllib.request, time def post(path, body): req=urllib.request.Request(''http://localhost:6333/collections/default/''+path, data=json.dum  [ok]\n- curl -s http://localhost:6333 ; echo; ss -ltnp 2>/dev/null | grep 6333 || netstat -ltnp 2>/dev/null | grep 6333  [ok]\n- python3 -c \" import json body={''ids'':[''e1d5e7b8-0000-4000-a000-000000000042''],''vectors'':[[0.3]*384],''payloads'':[{''document'':''probe3'',''metadata'':{''topic'':''x'',''ar  [ok]\nTools used in the summarized span: list_files, read_file, read_file_lines, replace_in_file, run_shell, todo_write, write_file", "user_messages": ["\u23f0 Scheduled run \u2014 Weekly research corpus -> Qdrant This automation is due now: carry out the task below immediately and produce the result. The schedule already exists \u2014 do not create or modify any scheduled tasks. Build this week''s research corpus and store it in Qdrant so my agents can retrieve it later. TOPICS \u2014 search each one separately, do not merge them into a single query: 1. Quantum computing: algorithms, error correction, hardware, quantum ML 2. Materials science: DFT, ML interatomic potentials, crystal structure generation 3. ML systems: inference efficiency, quantization, MoE arch\u2026"], "user_messages_dropped": 0, "created_at": 1787267686.0825255, "model_used": "ollama:qwen3.8-27b:latest", "trimmed": false}');
INSERT INTO sessions VALUES('2dfd699c-f71','/home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace','ollama:qwen3.8-27b:latest','auto','Tell me about openEvolve','fastchat',884,NULL,'[]',0,0,NULL,NULL,'openEvolve Overview',0,'2026-08-22 00:50:49','{}','{"boundary_index": 773, "summary_text": "# Compaction Summary\n\n## 1. Primary request and intent\n\nThe user is building **opensciencelab**, an open-source drug-discovery + materials-science platform combining OpenEvolve (evolutionary optimization), quantum chemistry (PySCF, MACE, CHGNet), and structure prediction (Boltz-2, Chai-1, ESMFold) behind a single adapter/orchestration layer with auditable provenance and budgeted compute.\n\n**Standing constraints (outlive all turns):**\n- Must be **open-source, local-first, reproducibility-pinned**\n- Must NOT evolve the physics \u2014 LLM edits code that *calls* QM tools, not basis-set coefficients\n- Layered/budgeted compute is non-negotiable (fast surrogate inner loop, DFT/MLIP middle, FEP+/CCSD(T) outer)\n- The active directive is **\"proceed with the buildout\"** \u2014 write working code, not just documentation\n- Budget charging happens in exactly one place: `Adapter.run`. Inner `_exec` calls are uncharged.\n- **Runtime: Docker**, on a **Strix Halo (gfx1151)** workstation with a **GPU** \u2014 ROCm (preferred over Vulkan)\n- **No shell tool available** in this session; verification is by strict code audit + grep, not by running pytest\n- **Phase 0 done. Phase 1 done. Phase 2 is ACTIVE**\n\n## 2. Key concepts and decisions\n\n**Architecture:**\n- Every capability is an `Adapter`. All calls funnel through `Adapter.run(manifest, budget, **inputs) -> Bundle` \u2014 single choke point for budget charging, artifact stamping, manifest recording.\n- Services own a `Budget`, pull adapters from the `registry` singleton.\n- Circular import resolution: `manifest.py` is self-contained; `base.py` re-exports from it. NOT the reverse.\n\n**Tiered scoring:**\n- Tier 0: RDKit-free surrogate (unlimited), QED-like desirability from SMILES-lite\n- Tier 1: MACE/CHGNet ML interatomic potentials (metered) \u2014 real backends in Phase 2\n- Tier 2: PySCF DFT / FEP+ (scarcity-budgeted) \u2014 real backend in Phase 2\n- Multi-objective Pareto via OpenEvolve\n\n**Budget charging (final):** `Adapter.run` is the ONLY place budget is charged. Inner `_exec` calls are uncharged. Optimizer adapter declares `{0:0, 1:0, 2:0}` (evaluator costs settled by ScoreService).\n\n**Phase 1 confirmed decisions:**\n- Boltz-2: `boltz` v2.2.1 on PyPI, Python >=3.10,<3.13. CLI: `boltz predict input.yaml -o dir`.\n- Chai-1: PyPI package `chai_lab` (underscore), pin `0.6.1`. Entry: `chai_lab.chai1.run_inference`.\n- ProteinMPNN: CLI `proteinmpnn --pdb-path <backbone.pdb> --out-folder <dir>`. Emits `predicted_sequence.jsonl`.\n- RFdiffusion NOT in the ROCm image. Keeps MPNN re-impose path.\n- `OPENSCIENCELAB_DEVICE` default is empty (auto-detect), NOT `auto`.\n- Docker base: `rocm/pytorch:rocm6.4_ubuntu24.04_py3.12_pytorch_stable` + `HSA_OVERRIDE_GFX_VERSION=11.5.1`.\n- Pip order: boltz \u2192 chai_lab==0.6.1 \u2192 proteinmpnn>=0.1.3 \u2192 rdkit \u2192 numpy<2.\n\n**Phase 2 decisions (implemented / verified):**\n- **MACE:** Package is `mace-torch` (=0.3.16). `MACECalculator(model_path=...)` from `mace.calculators` is stable; `mace_mp()` from `mace.calculators.foundation_models` is newer. Code uses `mace_mp()` first with `MACECalculator` fallback.\n- **CHGNet:** Package is `chgnet` (latest 0.4.2). `from ase.calculators.chgnet import CHGNet` \u2014 standard ASE calculator.\n- **PySCF:** Tier 2 DFT backend. `pyscf.gto.M` IS a valid shortcut function (verified against source). Standard pattern `mol = pyscf.gto.M(atom=..., basis=...); mf = pyscf.dft.RKS(mol); mf.kernel()` is correct. No bug.\n- **OpenEvolve:** Package is `openevolve` on PyPI. Latest: **0.1.0**. Repo: `algorithmicsuperintelligence/openevolve`.\n  - API (confirmed from `api.py` on GitHub): `run_evolution(initial_program_code, evaluator_fn, config, iterations, output_dir, ...) -> EvolutionResult`\n  - Evaluator is a callable `(program_path: str) -> metrics_dict`\n  - **CRITICAL (confirmed this session):** OpenEvolve''s `evaluator.py` uses `subprocess` \u2014 closures over Budget/bound-method will **silently break** in a real run. In-process budget tracking is LOST in the subprocess worker.\n\n**NEW \u2014 Two-stage scoring design (this session):**\nBecause OpenEvolve runs evaluator in a subprocess (no closure over Budget), the design is:\n1. **During OpenEvolve''s loop** (subprocess): evaluator is a **self-contained script** (`_OPENEVOLVE_EVALUATOR_SRC`) that imports the tier-0 surrogate scoring inline and returns a `combined_score` dict. Free, unlimited, no budget.\n2. **After OpenEvolve returns** (in-process): take the best program''s candidates, score them with the real `evaluator` callback (Tier 1/2, proper budget charging via `Adapter.run`).\nThis preserves the single-charging-point invariant while still using OpenEvolve''s evolution loop effectively.\n\n**Canonical tokenizer location:** SMILES-lite tokenizer (`_atom_tokens`), `_SYMBOL_TO_Z`, HBA/HBD atom sets live in `backends.py`. `scoring.py` imports from there.\n\n**ScoreService:** `model: Optional[str] = None` parameter on `ScoreService.score()` for selecting \"mace\" vs \"chgnet\" tier-1.\n\n## 3. Artifacts and files\n\nWorkspace root: `/home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab/`\n\n| Path | Role | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| `pyproject.toml` | Project config; v0.0.1, Apache-2.0, Python >=3.9. `structure` + `qm` extras (mace-torch, chgnet, pyscf, openevolve) | Stable |\n| `opensciencelab/__init__.py` | Package init; re-exports services, types, report, preflight | Stable |\n| `opensciencelab/__main__.py` | `python -m opensciencelab` \u2192 `cli.main()` | Stable |\n| `opensciencelab/base.py` | Shared types, `Adapter` base, `registry` singleton | Stable |\n| `opensciencelab/manifest.py` | `Manifest`, `Budget`, `BudgetExceeded`, `RunDirectory`; 303 lines | Stable |\n| `opensciencelab/services.py` | Four facades; `default_services()`; owns Budget; `model=` param on ScoreService | Stable |\n| `opensciencelab/cli.py` | CLI: `demo`, `score`, `optimize`, `preflight`, `registry`, `gpucheck` | Stable \u2014 `_cmd_score` is the subprocess target for tier-0 |\n| `opensciencelab/report.py` | 5-section markdown memo | Stable |\n| `opensciencelab/preflight.py` | Guardrails. Section 5 \"quantum backend availability\" | Stable |\n| `opensciencelab/backends.py` | Real backend wrappers (~634 lines). MACE, CHGNet, PySCF, ProteinMPNN CLI, `element_types_of`, SMILES-lite tokenizer | Stable |\n| `opensciencelab/gpucheck.py` | GPU verification | Stable |\n| `opensciencelab/adapters/__init__.py` | Import triggers registration of all 8 adapters | Stable |\n| `opensciencelab/adapters/structure.py` | `Boltz2Adapter` + `Chai1Adapter` | Stable |\n| `opensciencelab/adapters/design.py` | `RFDiffusionAdapter` + `ProteinMPNNAdapter` | Stable |\n| `opensciencelab/adapters/scoring.py` | Tier 0/1/2 scoring adapters; 403 lines | Stable |\n| `opensciencelab/adapters/optimize.py` | `OpenEvolveAdapter` \u2014 real path (OpenEvolve) + offline fallback. **~645 lines. ACTIVELY BEING MODIFIED this session.** Two-stage design implemented: subprocess evaluator for loop, in-process budgeted scoring after. Docstring updated. | **IN PROGRESS** |\n| `opensciencelab/adapters/evaluators.py` | `tier_evaluator`, `multi_objective_evaluator` factories | Stable |\n| `opensciencelab/tests.py` | Phase 2 tests (~14.6 KB) | Stable |\n| `smoke_run.py` | One-shot end-to-end check | Stable |\n| `docker/Dockerfile` | ROCm gfx1151 image; Phase 2 pip installs | Stable |\n| `docker/docker-run.sh` | Docker run wrapper; GPU device flags | Stable |\n| `README.md` | Philosophy, quickstart, architecture, roadmap | Needs Phase 2 QM section |\n| `LICENSE` | Apache 2.0 | Stable |\n| `.gitignore` | Python + run-artifact ignores | Stable |\n\n**OpenEvolve source references fetched this session:**\n- `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/algorithmicsuperintelligence/openevolve/main/openevolve/api.py` \u2014 confirmed `run_evolution` signature, evaluator is `(program_path: str) -> metrics_dict`, mandatory metric is `combined_score`\n- `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/algorithmicsuperintelligence/openevolve/main/openevolve/openevolve_main.py` \u2014 404, does not exist\n- DeepWiki quick-start guide \u2014 confirmed subprocess worker execution\n\n## 4. Errors and fixes\n\n1. **`apply_unified_diff` / `apply_patch` failed multiple times** (earlier sessions): \"Unified diff has no hunks\" / \"Patch context does not match\". **Fix:** Switched to `replace_in_file` for all edits.\n\n2. **`openevolve_main.py` 404:** The initial source fetch target was wrong. **Fix:** Found the correct API in `api.py` on the `main` branch of the repo.\n\n3. **OpenEvolve subprocess evaluator breaks closures:** Discovered that OpenEvolve runs evaluators in subprocess workers, meaning a Python closure over `Adapter.run`''s bound Budget would be silently lost. **Fix:** Designed two-stage scoring \u2014 self-contained inline evaluator (tier-0, free) for the subprocess loop, then in-process budgeted scoring after the loop returns. Implementation in progress.\n\n4. **PySCF \"bug\" (prior session) was a false alarm:** `pyscf.gto.M` is a valid shortcut, not a partial-function factory. Verified against source. No code change needed.\n\n## 5. All user messages\n\n(From prior compaction \u2014 preserved for audit-trail)\n- Initial request: build opensciencelab platform with OpenEvolve + QM + structure prediction\n- \"proceed with the buildout\" \u2014 write working code\n- Standing constraints on budget, layered compute, open-source, local-first\n- Phase ordering: 0 \u2192 1 \u2192 2, each with specific deliverables\n- Docker on Strix Halo gfx1151, ROCm preferred\n- No shell tool; verify by code audit\n\n(From current session \u2014 no explicit user messages; assistant was autonomously continuing Phase 2 buildout per the standing \"proceed with the buildout\" directive.)\n\n## 6. Pending tasks\n\n- **`_OPENEVOLVE_EVALUATOR_SRC`** \u2014 the self-contained evaluator source string that OpenEvolve''s subprocess", "working_state": "## Working state (extracted mechanically from tool records)\nTools used in the summarized span: grep, read_file, read_file_lines, replace_in_file, web_fetch", "user_messages": ["Tell me about openEvolve", "Tell me about openEvolve", "how can I combine this with quantum chemistry. I want to work with drug discovery and material science", "In one sentence, what is the capital of France?", "are their opensource versions of alphafold and claude-science?", "how can I get my version up to par with claude-science polish?", "Let''s create a buildout/roadmap to have an opensource version of alphafold and claude science?", "proceed with the buildout", "What should be done next?", "what is the next phase to work on?", "phase 0 is good. use docker and this workstation is a strix halo so there''s a gpu. Either vulkan or rocm", "\u23f0 Wake \u2014 the timer you set has fired (note: no-op). Continue where you left off.", "where is the code from the first two phases?", "okay let''s continue to the next phase"], "user_messages_dropped": 0, "created_at": 1787356490.6663947, "model_used": "ollama:qwen3.8-27b:latest", "trimmed": false}');
