INSERT INTO sessions VALUES('__run__run-8138867439','/home/iconbaypark2900/OpenWorker/__task__task-c6cf366b90','ollama:qwen3.8-27b:latest','interactive','⏰ Scheduled run — Job matches + tailored drafts','research',61,NULL,'[]',0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,'2026-08-21 13:03:56','{"tools": ["grep", "list_files", "read_file", "read_file_lines", "remember", "todo_write", "web_fetch", "web_search", "write_file"], "commands": []}','{"boundary_index": 22, "summary_text": "## Primary request and intent\n\nThis is a **scheduled, unattended automation job** (runs on a fixed schedule; the user should not create/modify the schedule). Its standing task:\n\n1. Read `resume.txt` in the workspace to establish candidate profile (background, seniority, domain, eligibility).\n2. **Continuity first**: list workspace files, read the 1\u20132 most recent prior `jobs-YYYY-MM-DD.md` outputs, carry forward live items, mark closed/resolved ones, and spend search budget on what is genuinely NEW since the last run. Never re-report an unchanged item as fresh.\n3. Search the web (allowed, no approval needed) for openings posted **roughly the last day**, in two categories:\n   - **Standard roles** matching the profile (seniority, domain, technical strengths).\n   - **Fellowships/residencies that function as paid jobs** (AI/ML residencies, research fellowships with salary/stipend, industry fellowships, government/think-tank technical fellowships). Exclude funding-only grants for independent work (those go to a separate weekly digest). Test: working *for* an org \u2192 include; receiving money for own project \u2192 exclude.\n4. For each match record: organisation, role title, standard vs. fellowship, location/remote policy, salary/stipend if stated, link, fit assessment (specific resume evidence + genuine gaps). Record cohort deadlines for fellowships.\n5. Rank by fit; keep only plausible matches (5 strong > 20 padded; 3 is fine if the day is thin).\n6. For the **top 3 matches**, create `drafts/` subfolder with:\n   - `cover-letter-<organisation>.md` \u2014 tailored to that posting, real resume evidence, what the org actually does.\n   - `resume-tweaks-<organisation>.md` \u2014 which bullets to lead with, rephrasing in posting''s language, what to cut.\n7. Save the shortlist as `jobs-YYYY-MM-DD.md` with fellowships and standard roles clearly labelled.\n8. **Never submit an application or contact anyone** \u2014 produce files only.\n9. **Never invent experience, credentials, or dates** not in the resume.\n10. **Hard constraints**: Do NOT use `run_shell`, `ls`, `cat`, `curl`, or Python scripts. Do NOT reach into `~/Documents/`. The run is unattended; shell commands halt execution. Web search IS allowed.\n11. **WORK, DON''T NARRATE**: do not end the turn to describe what is about to be done. Carry each step through. The run is not finished until the output file exists in the workspace \u2014 write it as the final action every time, even if a step failed. A file recording \"search returned nothing useful for X\" is a success; no file at all is a failure.\n\n## Key concepts and decisions\n\n- **Candidate profile** (from `resume.txt`): Jonathan Beale, ML Solutions Architect at Hewani (remote, Apr 2025\u2013Present). Former AI/ML Engineer at Mutual of Omaha (remote). ~2.5 yrs production ML. Tech stack: GCP Vertex AI (Feature Store, Matching Engine, AI Platform), RAG with LLMs/SLMs, ETL pipelines, REST inference APIs, Python, PyTorch, LangChain, Docker, GCP. Quantum-classical ML research (Hetionet knowledge graph, Neo4j/NetworkX, Qiskit/PennyLane), post-quantum RNG. No degree listed. No publications. No master''s/PhD.\n- **Fellowship vs. grant distinction**: The test is whether the candidate works *for* an organisation (\u2192 include) vs. receives money for their own independent project (\u2192 exclude, goes to separate weekly grant digest).\n- **Continuity model**: Outputs accumulate; each run reads prior `jobs-YYYY-MM-DD.md` files to avoid re-reporting stale items and to track state changes (e.g., \"X, first flagged <date>, is now <state>\").\n- **Deadline tracking**: Fellowships with fixed cohort deadlines must have the deadline recorded because they close on a date, not when filled.\n- **Prior runs identified**: `jobs-2026-08-18.md`, `jobs-2026-08-19.md`, `jobs-2026-08-20.md` exist in the workspace, along with many `drafts/` files from prior top-3 selections (AIAF, Anthropic, Baseten, CrowdStrike, CSC Generation, Databricks, Doma, Dragos, GovAI, Home Depot, and others).\n- **Horizon Fellowship 2027**: Confirmed deadline **August 30, 2026** (from horizonpublicservice.org). This is a technology-policy fellowship in DC \u2014 relevant as a government/think-tank technical fellowship.\n- **Search sources used**: Tavily (web search + extract), DuckDuckGo (web_search), direct page fetch (web_fetch).\n\n## Artifacts and files\n\n| Path | Role | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `resume.txt` | Candidate profile source | Read in full; establishes ~2.5 yrs ML, GCP/RAG/LLM/quantum-ML, no degree. |\n| `jobs-2026-08-20.md` | Most recent prior shortlist | Read; contains active openings and fellowship deadlines carried forward. |\n| `jobs-2026-08-19.md` | Prior shortlist | Read; provides context on what was already reported. |\n| `jobs-2026-08-18.md` | Prior shortlist | Read; Toptal AI/ML Engineer role and others listed. |\n| `drafts/` (many files) | Prior cover letters & resume tweaks | At least 11+ files visible (AIAF, Anthropic, Baseten, CrowdStrike, CSC, Databricks, Doma, Dragos, GovAI, Home Depot, etc.). From prior runs'' top-3 selections. |\n| `jobs-YYYY-MM-DD.md` (today''s date) | **Output to be created** | The shortlist file for today''s run. **Not yet written.** |\n| `drafts/cover-letter-<org>.md` + `resume-tweaks-<org>.md` (top 3) | **Output to be created** | Tailored drafts for top 3 new/changed matches. **Not yet written.** |\n\n### Key search results found (not yet written to file):\n\n- **SAI Systems Intl., Inc.** \u2014 AI Agents Engineer (LLM/OpenAI/RAG), Remote US, Contract. Found via Dice. Posting date: \"Today\" (Aug 21).\n- **Clover Health** \u2014 Senior ML Engineer, Remote. Found via Dice. Details partially extracted.\n- **Tether** \u2014 Remote AI Research Engineer, RL agents in production. Found via weworkremotely.\n- **Horizon Fellowship 2027** \u2014 Technology policy fellowship, DC. Deadline **Aug 30, 2026**. Confirmed via horizonpublicservice.org.\n- **Prime Intellect** \u2014 AI Research Residency program. Listed on builtinsf.com. Extract returned mostly page chrome, not substantive details.\n- **Open Style Lab AI Research Residency** (Columbia) \u2014 This is a news article about a professor being selected; NOT an open application. Likely not relevant.\n\n## Errors and fixes\n\n- **Tavily extract on builtinsf.com** (Prime Intellect AI Research Residency): Returned `undefined` raw content and mostly BuiltIn.com boilerplate. Did not yield a usable job description. The assistant would need an alternative approach or skip this listing.\n- **No user corrections** were issued in this session (the user''s message was the original job spec; the assistant was mid-execution).\n- **No shell-command violations**: The assistant correctly avoided `run_shell`, `ls`, `cat`, `curl` and instead used `list_files`, `read_file`, `web_search`, `web_fetch`, and Tavily MCP tools.\n\n## All user messages\n\n1. **(The sole user message \u2014 the scheduled job spec)**: Full task description covering: read resume.txt, continuity check against prior `jobs-YYYY-MM-DD.md` files, search last-day openings in two categories (standard + paid fellowships/residencies, exclude funding-only grants), record structured details per match, rank by fit (5 strong > 20 padded, 3 is fine if thin), create `drafts/` with cover letter + resume tweaks for top 3, save as `jobs-YYYY-MM-DD.md`, never submit applications, never invent experience, hard constraint against shell commands, \"WORK DON''T NARRATE\" directive, and the continuity-first protocol.\n\n## Pending tasks\n\nFrom the todo list the assistant created (and the remaining work per the job spec):\n\n1. ~~Review prior briefs + resume (continuity baseline)~~ \u2014 **done** (read 2026-08-18, 08-19, 08-20 briefs + resume)\n2. **Search new (last ~day) standard roles matching the profile** \u2014 **in_progress** (found SAI Systems, Clover Health, Tether; may need additional search)\n3. **Check state changes: Claude Corps re-open, rolling residencies still live** \u2014 **pending** (was flagged in prior briefs for September; needs verification)\n4. **Search new fellowships/residencies with open deadlines** \u2014 **in_progress** (Horizon Fellowship Aug 30 confirmed; Prime Intellect residency found but details unavailable; need to check if any other fellowships have new openings)\n5. **Write drafts/ for top 3 new matches** \u2014 **pending** (cover-letter + resume-tweaks per org)\n6. **Write and save `jobs-YYYY-MM-DD.md`** (today''s date) \u2014 **pending** (this is the mandatory final action)\n\n## Current work\n\nThe assistant was in the **search-and-verify phase**, roughly 60% through the job:\n\n- Continuity reading: **complete** (3 prior briefs read).\n- Web searches: **partially complete**. Found several candidates (SAI Systems AI Agents Engineer, Clover Health Sr ML Engineer, Tether AI Research Engineer, Horizon Fellowship 2027, Prime Intellect residency). The Tavily extract for Prime Intellect failed (garbage content). Horizon Fellowship deadline (Aug 30) was confirmed.\n- State-change checks (Claude Corps re-open, rolling residencies): **not yet started**.\n- Fit assessment and ranking: **not yet done**.\n- Draft creation (`drafts/`): **not yet started**.\n- Final output file (`jobs-YYYY-MM-DD.md`): **not yet written**. This is the critical missing deliverable \u2014 without it the run is a failure per the job spec.\n\nThe workspace date context is **August 21, 2026** (inferred from the \"posted Today\" on the SAI Systems listing and the search timestamps). So the output file should be `jobs-2026-08-21.md`.\n\n## Next step\n\n**Complete the remaining search/verification, then write the two output artifacts:**\n\n1. Finish verifying the state of items flagged in prior briefs (Claude Corps re-open in September, any rolling residencies still live", "working_state": "## Working state (extracted mechanically from tool records)\nTools used in the summarized span: list_files, mcp__tavily__tavily-tavily_extract, mcp__tavily__tavily-tavily_search, read_file, todo_write, web_fetch, web_search", "user_messages": ["\u23f0 Scheduled run \u2014 Job matches + tailored drafts This automation is due now: carry out the task below immediately and produce the result. The schedule already exists \u2014 do not create or modify any scheduled tasks. Find roles worth applying for, based on my resume. Your resume is staged in your own workspace as resume.txt (plain text, already extracted from the PDF) \u2014 read it with your file tools, by that plain filename, and use it to establish background, seniority, technical domain and eligibility. Do NOT use run_shell, ls, cat, curl or a Python script, and do not try to reach into ~/Documents\u2026"], "user_messages_dropped": 0, "created_at": 1787301921.6172407, "model_used": "ollama:qwen3.8-27b:latest", "trimmed": false}');
INSERT INTO sessions VALUES('__run__run-e7dc20dbe2','/home/iconbaypark2900/OpenWorker/__task__task-717e4360ea','ollama:qwen3.8-27b:latest','interactive','⏰ Scheduled run — Repo activity brief','repo-ops',22,NULL,'[]',0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,'2026-08-21 13:14:25','{"tools": ["grep", "list_files", "read_file", "read_file_lines", "remember", "run_shell", "todo_write", "web_fetch", "web_search", "write_file"], "commands": []}','{"boundary_index": 8, "summary_text": "## Primary request and intent\n\nScheduled automation (runs daily, outputs accumulate as a running record) to produce a 24-hour repo-activity brief across 10 repos under `iconbaypark2900/`. Standing constraints:\n\n- **Budget: max 12 tool calls.** If the cap is hit, state which repos were not reached rather than silently truncating.\n- **No guessing:** if a commit message is too terse to summarise honestly, fetch file contents via `github-get_file_contents`. Never infer behaviour from a subject line alone.\n- **Stalled-work flag:** surface any repo with no commits in 7+ days that *did* have recent activity before that gap.\n- **WIP flag:** explicitly call out commits whose message is only \"WIP\" or equivalent with no other context.\n- **Continuity is mandatory:** before any searching, read the 1\u20132 most recent prior reports (same `repo-activity-YYYY-MM-DD.md` naming pattern) and carry forward open threads. Never re-report an unchanged item as new. If a previously flagged item changed state, say so explicitly (\"X, first flagged <date>, is now <state>\").\n- **If nothing changed anywhere:** say exactly that in one line; do not pad.\n- **Do not create or modify any scheduled tasks.**\n- **Output file:** `repo-activity-2026-08-21.md` (today''s date).\n\n## Key concepts and decisions\n\n- The 10 repos are: `dcode-stack`, `workstation-stack`, `ragtradesystem`, `sigma`, `liaison-agentSystem`, `qgg_research`, `materialScience`, `setup`, `polymarket_btc`, `sourcelab_ai_production_scaffold` (all under `iconbaypark2900/`).\n- **Critical finding from the 2026-08-20 run:** 9 of the 10 repos return **HTTP 404** on the GitHub API and do not appear in the account''s public repo list. They are **private** and not accessible via the current API token/method. The only verifiable repo is **`liaison-agentSystem`**.\n- This means the practical search budget should be spent on `liaison-agentSystem` (the only reachable repo) and confirming whether the 404 situation has changed since the prior run.\n- The workspace also contains helper scripts (`brief.py`, `fetch_activity.py`, `fetch_commits.py`, `repo_ops_check.py`) that were presumably used to attempt bulk fetching in prior runs.\n\n## Artifacts and files\n\n| Path | Role | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `repo-activity-2026-08-18.md` | Prior report (oldest in workspace) | Not yet read this session |\n| `repo-activity-2026-08-19.md` | Prior report | Not yet read this session |\n| `repo-activity-2026-08-20.md` | **Most recent prior report \u2014 read this session** | Key content: only `liaison-agentSystem` was verifiable; 9 repos 404''d (private). Window covered since ~2026-08-19 12:00 UTC. |\n| `brief.py`, `fetch_activity.py`, `fetch_commits.py`, `repo_ops_check.py` | Helper scripts in workspace | Purpose unclear this session; may have been used for prior bulk-fetch attempts |\n| `repo-activity-2026-08-21.md` | **Target output (not yet created)** | Must be written this session |\n\n## Errors and fixes\n\n- **9/10 repos return HTTP 404** (discovered in the 2026-08-20 run, carried forward as context). Root cause: repos are private and the current API access cannot see them. This is **not a transient error** \u2014 it has persisted across at least the 08-20 run (and likely 08-19 and earlier, given the scripts present). No fix has been applied; the workaround is to focus budget on the one reachable repo and note the 404 situation in the report.\n- No user corrections or feedback in this session yet.\n\n## All user messages\n\n1. **(Scheduled trigger \u2014 full task spec):** \"Summarise what moved in my repositories in the last 24 hours.\" Lists all 10 repos, the 3-step method (list commits \u2192 optional file fetch \u2192 group by repo), the two flags (stalled 7+ days, WIP-only), the 12-call budget rule, the output filename pattern, and the continuity protocol (read prior reports first, carry forward, don''t re-report unchanged items, state changed state explicitly).\n\n## Pending tasks\n\nFrom the todo list (state at compaction):\n\n| Todo | Status |\n|---|---|\n| Read most recent prior report for continuity | **in_progress** (read 08-20; 08-19 possibly worth a skim but lower priority) |\n| Check commits in all 10 repos (last 24h, 7-day signal) | pending |\n| Write `repo-activity-2026-08-21.md` and summarize | pending |\n\nNo other user-requested tasks are queued.\n\n## Current work\n\nThe assistant had just finished reading `repo-activity-2026-08-20.md` (the most recent prior report) and confirmed the key continuity fact: only `liaison-agentSystem` is reachable; the other 9 are 404/private. The todo for \"Read most recent prior report\" was still marked `in_progress`. **No `github-list_commits` calls have been made yet this session.** Tool calls used so far: **3** (todo_write, list_files, read_file). Remaining budget: **9**.\n\nThe immediate next action was interrupted at the point of transitioning to commit-checking.\n\n## Next step\n\n1. Mark \"Read most recent prior report\" as completed.\n2. **Spend the remaining budget (9 calls) on `github-list_commits` for `liaison-agentSystem`** (the only verifiable repo) \u2014 last 24 h and also look back ~7 days to detect the stalled-work flag. One call should suffice for the 24 h window; a second call (or date-range parameter) for the 7-day signal.\n3. For the 9 private repos: make a **single confirming call** (or note in the report) that the 404 condition persists \u2014 since the prior report already established this, per the continuity rule it should be noted as \"unchanged since 2026-08-20\" rather than re-discovered. A lightweight batch check (or simply stating the continuity fact if the API token has not changed) is acceptable.\n4. Write `repo-activity-2026-08-21.md` grouped by repo, flag stalled/WIP items, note the 9-repo 404 situation as a carried-forward finding, and confirm which repos (if any) were not reached due to the 12-call cap.", "working_state": "## Working state (extracted mechanically from tool records)\nTools used in the summarized span: list_files, read_file, todo_write", "user_messages": ["\u23f0 Scheduled run \u2014 Repo activity brief This automation is due now: carry out the task below immediately and produce the result. The schedule already exists \u2014 do not create or modify any scheduled tasks. Summarise what moved in my repositories in the last 24 hours. REPOS \u2014 check these, they are the ones under active work: iconbaypark2900/dcode-stack iconbaypark2900/workstation-stack iconbaypark2900/ragtradesystem iconbaypark2900/sigma iconbaypark2900/liaison-agentSystem iconbaypark2900/qgg_research iconbaypark2900/materialScience iconbaypark2900/setup iconbaypark2900/polymarket_btc iconbaypark2\u2026"], "user_messages_dropped": 0, "created_at": 1787318062.3247018, "model_used": "ollama:qwen3.8-27b:latest", "trimmed": false}');
