INSERT INTO sessions VALUES('__run__run-b69cb8e824','/home/iconbaypark2900/OpenWorker/__task__task-717e4360ea','ollama:qwen3.8-27b:latest','interactive','⏰ Scheduled run — Repo activity brief','repo-ops',21,NULL,'[]',0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,'2026-08-22 09:54:05','{"tools": ["grep", "list_files", "mcp__github__github-get_file_contents", "mcp__github__github-list_commits", "read_file", "read_file_lines", "remember", "run_shell", "todo_write", "web_fetch", "web_search", "write_file"], "commands": []}','{"boundary_index": 7, "summary_text": "**Primary request and intent**\n\nScheduled automation (runs on a schedule; do NOT create/modify scheduled tasks). Task: produce a repo-activity brief for the last 24 hours across 10 specific repos under `iconbaypark2900/`. Deliverable: `repo-activity-<YYYY-MM-DD>.md` in the workspace.\n\nStanding constraints:\n- **Budget: at most 12 tool calls total.** If the limit is hit, state which repos were not reached rather than silently truncating.\n- Do NOT guess commit content from subject alone; only call `github-get_file_contents` when a message is too terse.\n- Group report by repo: what changed + why it matters.\n- Flag repos with no commits in 7+ days that had prior activity (stalled work).\n- Flag WIP-only or contextless commit messages.\n- **Continuity is mandatory and comes first:** read prior briefs, carry forward live items, explicitly note state changes (\"X, first flagged <date>, is now <state>\"), and never re-report an unchanged item as new.\n- If nothing changed anywhere, say exactly that in one line \u2014 do not pad.\n\n**Key concepts and decisions**\n\n- 10 target repos (all under `iconbaypark2900`): `dcode-stack`, `workstation-stack`, `ragtradesystem`, `sigma`, `liaison-agentSystem`, `qgg_research`, `materialScience`, `setup`, `polymarket_btc`, `sourcelab_ai_production_scaffold`.\n- Prior brief (2026-08-20) revealed a critical fact: **9 of the 10 repos returned HTTP 404 on the GitHub API** \u2014 they are private and inaccessible to the automation''s token. Only 1 repo was verifiable in that run. This is a recurring access problem, not a one-off.\n- The 2026-08-20 brief specifically listed the 9 failing repos as: dcode-stack, workstation-stack, ragtradesystem, sigma, qgg_research, materialScience, setup, polymarket_btc, sourcelab_ai_production_scaffold. The one that *was* accessible (likely `liaison-agentSystem`) was the only one successfully checked.\n- This access constraint likely still holds and should be flagged rather than re-attempting all 10 blindly (which would waste the 12-call budget).\n\n**Artifacts and files**\n\n| File | Role | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `repo-activity-2026-08-18.md` | Prior brief | Exists in workspace; not yet read this session |\n| `repo-activity-2026-08-19.md` | Prior brief | Exists in workspace; not yet read this session |\n| `repo-activity-2026-08-20.md` | Most recent prior brief (continuity anchor) | Read this session. Key finding: 9/10 repos 404 (private), only 1 verifiable. Window was since 2026-08-19 ~12:00 UTC. |\n| `repo-activity-2026-08-22.md` | **Target output** (not yet written) | Expected deliverable for this run |\n\n**Errors and fixes**\n\n- **9 repos return 404 on GitHub API** (observed in 2026-08-20 brief). They are private; the automation''s credentials cannot access them. This was not \"fixed\" \u2014 it was reported. The implication for this run: attempting `github-list_commits` on those 9 repos will likely fail again and burn tool calls. The continuity instruction says to carry forward known issues, not re-discover them.\n- No other errors encountered yet this session (work is very early).\n\n**All user messages**\n\n1. *(Scheduled run prompt)* \u2014 Full task spec: summarise last-24h repo activity across 10 listed repos, with method (list_commits \u2192 optional get_file_contents), grouping rules, flagging rules (7+ day stalls, WIP-only), 12-tool-call budget, output filename pattern, and a detailed continuity protocol (read prior briefs first, carry forward, mark state changes, never re-report unchanged items). Emphasises: \"do not create or modify any scheduled tasks.\"\n\n**Pending tasks**\n\n- Complete the 24-hour commit check across the 10 repos (respecting the 404/access issue from prior brief).\n- Check for stalled repos (7+ days no commits but had prior activity) and WIP-only commit messages.\n- Write the final report to `repo-activity-2026-08-22.md` with proper continuity language.\n- Stay within the 12-tool-call budget.\n\n**Current work**\n\nThe assistant is in the **continuity read** phase, step 1 of the mandated sequence. It has:\n- Created a 4-item todo list (in_progress: \"Review prior briefs for continuity\").\n- Listed workspace files \u2192 found 3 prior briefs (08-18, 08-19, 08-20).\n- Started reading `repo-activity-2026-08-20.md` (most recent); read the first portion confirming the 9-repo 404 issue.\n- **Has NOT yet** read `repo-activity-2026-08-19.md` (the instructions say read the 1\u20132 most recent).\n- **Has NOT yet** begun any `github-list_commits` calls.\n\nTool calls used so far: **2** (list_files, read_file). Remaining: **10** of 12.\n\n**Next step**\n\nFinish the continuity pass (optionally skim `repo-activity-2026-08-19.md` if budget allows \u2014 that''s 1 more call, 3 total), then proceed to `github-list_commits` for the repos. Given the 9-repo 404 pattern from the prior brief, the efficient path is:\n1. (Optional) Read `repo-activity-2026-08-19.md` for any additional state context \u2014 1 call.\n2. `github-list_commits` on `iconbaypark2900/liaison-agentSystem` (the known-accessible repo) for the last 24 h \u2014 1 call.\n3. `github-list_commits` on a small sample of the 9 private repos to confirm the 404s persist (or skip and carry forward the prior finding, saving calls).\n4. Write `repo-activity-2026-08-22.md` with continuity language (\"9 repos, first flagged 2026-08-20, still 404 / inaccessible\") and any genuine new activity.\n\nThis keeps well within the 12-call budget while honouring the continuity mandate.", "working_state": "## Working state (extracted mechanically from tool records)\nTools used in the summarized span: list_files, read_file, todo_write", "user_messages": ["\u23f0 Scheduled run \u2014 Repo activity brief This automation is due now: carry out the task below immediately and produce the result. The schedule already exists \u2014 do not create or modify any scheduled tasks. Summarise what moved in my repositories in the last 24 hours. REPOS \u2014 check these, they are the ones under active work: iconbaypark2900/dcode-stack iconbaypark2900/workstation-stack iconbaypark2900/ragtradesystem iconbaypark2900/sigma iconbaypark2900/liaison-agentSystem iconbaypark2900/qgg_research iconbaypark2900/materialScience iconbaypark2900/setup iconbaypark2900/polymarket_btc iconbaypark2\u2026"], "user_messages_dropped": 0, "created_at": 1787392442.4433982, "model_used": "ollama:qwen3.8-27b:latest", "trimmed": false}');
