INSERT INTO sessions VALUES('__run__run-7687c01ffc','/home/iconbaypark2900/OpenWorker/__task__task-1b2c4d3f13','ollama:qwen3.8-27b:latest','interactive','⏰ Scheduled run — Research papers — quantum, ML, recursive s','research',82,NULL,'[]',0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,'2026-08-22 10:18:44','{"tools": ["grep", "list_files", "read_file", "read_file_lines", "remember", "todo_write", "web_fetch", "web_search", "write_file"], "commands": []}','{"boundary_index": 29, "summary_text": "**Primary request and intent**\n\nScheduled (unattended) run of a recurring \"Research papers\" job. Standing instructions (outlive individual turns):\n\n- Find research papers published in the last 24 hours across three topics: (1) Quantum computing (algorithms, error correction, hardware, quantum ML), (2) Machine learning (architectures, training methods, reasoning, evaluation), (3) Recursive self-improvement (self-modifying agents, automated AI research, autonomous research loops).\n- **Must** use arXiv MCP tools (`search_papers`, `get_abstract`, `semantic_search`). **Must NOT** write Python scripts, use `run_shell`, or `curl` \u2014 shell commands stall unattended runs on human-approval.\n- If arXiv tools return nothing useful, fall back to the **web search tool** \u2014 never to shell.\n- For each paper: title, authors, link, and 2-3 sentences of the assistant''s own analysis (not abstract restatement).\n- Be selective; skip incremental variations. If a topic has nothing genuinely new, say so in one line.\n- **Deliverable:** Save result as `papers-YYYY-MM-DD.md` in the task workspace, grouped by three topics, most significant first. Writing that file is mandatory \u2014 do not finish without it.\n- **Continuity rule (do FIRST):** Read 1-2 most recent prior outputs; carry forward what''s live; mark closed items; spend search budget on what is genuinely NEW since last run; explicitly note state changes (\"X, first flagged <date>, is now <state>\"); never re-report an unchanged item as fresh.\n- Do **not** create or modify scheduled tasks.\n\n**Key concepts and decisions**\n\n- **arXiv MCP `search_papers` OR-chain quirk:** Queries with multiple quoted phrases joined by OR (e.g., `\"quantum error correction\" OR \"quantum computing\" algorithm OR hardware`) return `total_results: 0`. Simple single-quoted-phrase queries work. **Always use focused single-phrase queries.**\n- **Date-filter behavior:** The `date_from` parameter filters by submission/announcement date and seemed unreliable for the target window. The assistant pivoted to sorting by date without explicit `date_from`/`date_to` filters, which returned results (20 papers per query, sorted descending by date).\n- **Target window:** Papers submitted on or around 2026-08-21, for output file `papers-2026-08-22.md`.\n- **Continuity anchors from prior runs** (read from `papers-2026-08-20.md` and `papers-2026-08-21.md`):\n  - **Blanc et al., \"Quantum Speedups Require Structure or Depth\"** (arXiv:2608.19158, FOCS 2026) \u2014 settled a quantum-complexity conjecture. Flagged 2026-08-20. Companion: Liu & Mutreja (Aaronson\u2013Ambainis almost-everywhere simulation, massively-parallel queries), flagged 2026-08-21.\n  - **SPADE / EnvHarness** \u2014 reported in prior runs.\n  - **Eureka''s math claim** \u2014 reported prior.\n  - **Phantom Gains** \u2014 reported prior.\n  - **AI4AI-Bench** (arXiv:2608.20318, Chi et al.) \u2014 **already reported** in prior outputs. Surfaced again in current search results; must NOT re-report.\n  - **ONEX** \u2014 reported prior.\n- **Borderline paper:** \"Architecture and Compilation Co-Design for High-Rate Quantum Product Codes on Neutral Atom Arrays\" (arXiv:2608.20164, Liu/Lin/Tan/Xu/Cong) \u2014 submitted 2026-08-20. Was in the prior reporting window but may not have been explicitly included in either prior output. Needs verification before deciding if it qualifies as new.\n- **Relevance filtering needed:** Some top-dated results are off-topic for the three target areas (e.g., \"Group-theoretic treatment of strong light-matter coupling\" is quantum optics/physics, not quantum computing; \"Information on trajectories: martingales and random times\" is pure math/probability, not ML).\n\n**Artifacts and files**\n\n| Path | Role | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| `papers-2026-08-16.md` | Prior output (earliest) | Exists in workspace; not read this run |\n| `papers-2026-08-18.md` | Prior output | Exists in workspace; not read this run |\n| `papers-2026-08-20.md` | Prior output (read this run) | Reports Blanc et al. (08-19 subms); SPAD/EnvHarness; Eureka; Phantom Gains; AI4AI-Bench; ONEX |\n| `papers-2026-08-21.md` | Prior output (read this run) | Reports Blanc companion (Liu & Mutreja); notes Blanc et al. flagged 08-20 now has companion |\n| `papers-2026-08-22.md` | **Target deliverable** | **Not yet created** |\n\n**Errors and fixes**\n\n- **OR-chain query syntax failure:** Initial arXiv searches used long OR-chains. All three topic queries returned `total_results: 0`. Fixed by switching to focused single-phrase queries (e.g., `\"quantum error correction\"`, `\"recursive self-improvement\"`), which returned results when sorted by date without date filters.\n- **Date-filter returning 0:** Queries with explicit `date_from: 2026-08-21` returned 0 results across all three topics. Workaround: dropped the date filter, sorted by date descending, and manually filter results by date. This successfully returned ~20 papers per query.\n- **Off-topic results in date-sorted lists:** Top results include papers outside the three target topics (quantum optics, pure math). Must filter by topical relevance before reporting.\n\n**All user messages**\n\n1. *(Scheduled-run prompt)* \u2014 \"Find research papers published in the last 24 hours across three topics: Quantum computing, Machine learning, Recursive self-improvement. Use arXiv MCP tools directly. Do NOT write a Python script, do NOT use run_shell or curl. If arxiv tool returns nothing useful, use the web search tool \u2014 never fall back to shell. For each paper give title, authors, link, 2-3 sentences on what is genuinely new. Be selective. Save as papers-YYYY-MM-DD.md. CONTINUITY: read prior outputs first, carry forward what''s live, never re-report unchanged items.\"\n\n**Pending tasks**\n\n- **Evaluate the ~20 papers returned per query** (from date-sorted, no-filter arXiv searches) for: (a) topical relevance to the three target areas, (b) publication date within the last-24-hours window (~2026-08-20/21), (c) whether they are already reported in prior outputs (AI4AI-Bench is confirmed already reported). Select genuinely new, significant papers.\n- **Verify arXiv:2608.20164** (neutral-atom QEC co-design) against prior outputs to confirm whether it was already reported.\n- **Read abstracts** (`get_abstract`) of any qualifying candidates and write 2-3 sentence original analysis for each.\n- **If arXiv yields nothing genuinely new for a topic**, fall back to the **web search tool** per standing instruction.\n- **Write `papers-2026-08-22.md`** \u2014 the mandatory deliverable. Group by three topics, most significant first. For any topic with nothing new, note it in one line. Include continuity notes (state changes from prior runs). **This file must be created before the run is complete.**\n- Do not create or modify scheduled tasks.\n\n**Current work**\n\nThe assistant completed the continuity pass (read both prior output files) and was actively **searching and filtering arXiv results**. It had just received tool results from three date-sorted queries (no explicit date filter):\n\n- `\"quantum error correction\"` (quant-ph, cs.QC) \u2192 20 papers, top: 2608.20340 (light-matter coupling \u2014 off-topic)\n- `\"recursive self-improvement\"` \u2192 20 papers, top: 2608.20318 (AI4AI-Bench \u2014 **already reported**, must skip)\n- `\"chain-of-thought\" OR \"reasoning model\"` (cs.LG, cs.CL) \u2192 20 papers, top: 2608.20337 (martingales \u2014 off-topic)\n\nThe assistant was about to **filter through the full result lists** to identify papers that are (a) genuinely within the last-24h window, (b) topically relevant, and (c) not already in prior reports. No candidates have been confirmed as new yet. The deliverable file has not been started.\n\n**Next step**\n\nScan the full 20-paper result lists from each of the three queries to identify candidates that are topically relevant, within the 2026-08-20/21 date window, and not already reported in prior outputs. For any qualifying candidates, call `get_abstract` to read the full abstract and write the 2-3 sentence analysis. If no genuinely new papers are found across all three topics after a reasonable set of queries (try 2-3 more single-phrase angles, e.g., `\"quantum machine learning\"`, `\"large language model\" training`, `\"automated\" \"AI research\"`), then either fall back to the web search tool or note the gap in one line per topic. Finally, **write `papers-2026-08-22.md`** with the three-topic structure, continuity notes, and the mandatory one-line \"nothing new\" notes where applicable.", "working_state": "## Working state (extracted mechanically from tool records)\nTools used in the summarized span: mcp__arxiv__arxiv-search_papers, read_file", "user_messages": ["\u23f0 Scheduled run \u2014 Research papers \u2014 quantum, ML, recursive self-improvement This automation is due now: carry out the task below immediately and produce the result. The schedule already exists \u2014 do not create or modify any scheduled tasks. Find research papers published in the last 24 hours across three topics: 1. Quantum computing \u2014 algorithms, error correction, hardware, quantum ML. 2. Machine learning \u2014 architectures, training methods, reasoning, evaluation. 3. Recursive self-improvement \u2014 self-modifying agents, automated AI research, models that improve their own capabilities, scaling of \u2026"], "user_messages_dropped": 0, "created_at": 1787388134.843299, "model_used": "ollama:qwen3.8-27b:latest", "trimmed": false}');
