INSERT INTO sessions VALUES('9c89361c-87a','/home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab','ollama:qwen3.8-27b:latest','custom','Phase 2, item 4 only. Read PHASE2.md first (it records items','builder',367,NULL,'[]',0,0,NULL,NULL,'I''ll start by reading the key files to understand the curren',0,'2026-08-23 19:59:10','{"tools": ["apply_unified_diff", "replace_in_file"], "commands": []}','{"boundary_index": 283, "summary_text": "**Primary request and intent**\n\nThe user is working through `openevolve_roadmap.md` phase by phase. **Phase 2 (all 4 items)** is fully closed (commit `34aa088`, branch `phase2-drug-and-materials`). The user then asked \"What is next to do?\" and selected **Phase 3, Item 2: AutoDock Vina adapter** \u2014 replacing the deterministic `_docking_surrogate` in `drugdiscovery.py` with a real subprocess-based AutoDock Vina adapter that:\n\n- Lives in `opensciencelab/docking.py` (the module name is already reserved in `scripts/drug_evolve_example.py:39`).\n- Exposes `vina_objective()` returning `Candidate -> Optional[float]` (higher-is-better affinity); returning `None` per-candidate triggers the existing surrogate fallback stamped `\"surrogate-offline\"`.\n- Gracefully degrades: if no `vina` binary or receptor PDBQT is available, the adapter reports unavailable and the evaluator falls back to surrogate.\n- Is testable without a real binary (tests use a fake `vina` script on PATH).\n- Includes 5 new tests, PHASE3.md documentation, and a commit.\n\n**Standing constraints (outlive all turns):**\n- Do NOT change `BaseAdapter.run()` or `OptimizeService.evolve()`.\n- Domain-agnostic: nothing in `adapters/` may branch on `kind == \"material\"` / `\"molecule\"`.\n- No new dependencies.\n- Do NOT regress `notes` provenance (item 2''s fix).\n- Do NOT re-implement Phase 2 items.\n- The \"real-adapter-or-stamped-surrogate\" discipline: real path must be honest, surrogate must be clearly stamped.\n\n**Key concepts and decisions**\n\n- **Reserved slot**: `scripts/drug_evolve_example.py:39` does `from opensciencelab.docking import vina_objective` \u2014 this module and function name are the contract. The adapter must fill this exact path.\n- **Contract**: `docking_fn: Optional[Callable[[Candidate], Optional[float]]]` \u2014 higher-is-better affinity (kcal/mol flipped to positive). `None` \u2192 evaluator uses `_docking_surrogate` stamped `\"surrogate-offline\"`.\n- **Environment**: No `vina` binary, no RDKit, no meeko, no openbabel, no `autodock-vina` pip package available. The real path can only be exercised via subprocess; tests must mock with a fake `vina` script.\n- **`ScoreVector`** (in `base.py`): has `.tier` (int), `.metrics` (dict), `.notes` (str). Tiers: `TIER_ZERO=0`, `TIER_ONE=1`, `TIER_TWO=2`.\n- **`Candidate`** (in `base.py`): dataclass with `.id`, `.kind` (default `\"molecule\"`), `.smi`, `.seq`, `.metadata`, `.notes`.\n- **`Budget`** (in `manifest.py`): `.costs` dict tier\u2192rate, `.remaining_for(tier, units)` non-mutating, `.spend(tier, units)` mutating.\n- **Vina output format**: Rows like `\" 1 -7.0 0.400 12.5\"` (mode, affinity_kcal, rmsd, energy). Parser extracts `(mode, affinity_kcal)`.\n- **`_optional_docking_fn()`** in the example script: checks `VINA_RECEPTOR_PDBQT` + `VINA_BINARY` env vars; if both present, instantiates `VinaAdapter` and returns `(fn, \"real\")`; else returns `(None, \"surrogate\")`.\n- **Test count discrepancy**: Prior compaction stated \"45 tests\" after Phase 2, but actual count at commit `34aa088` is **71**. After Phase 3 item 2: **76 tests** (71 + 5 new). PHASE3.md correctly states \"71 at 34aa088 + 5 new\".\n- **`propose_plan` was rejected** with error \"not in plan mode \u2014 proceed with the work directly\" \u2014 the user wants direct execution, not plan approval cycles.\n\n**Artifacts and files**\n\n| Path | Role | State |\n|------|------|-------|\n| `opensciencelab/docking.py` (~279 lines) | **NEW** \u2014 `VinaConfig` dataclass, `VinaAdapter` class (subprocess call to vina binary), `vina_objective()` factory, `_parse_vina_output()` pure parser, `_best_affinity()` helper, `_config_from_env()` (reads `VINA_RECEPTOR_PDBQT`, `VINA_BINARY`, `VINA_BOX` env vars). | **UNCOMMITTED** |\n| `scripts/drug_evolve_example.py` (~115\u2192~130 lines) | **MODIFIED** \u2014 added `_optional_docking_fn()` helper; replaced hard-coded docking import with conditional real-vs-surrogate logic; prints honest status (\"docking: real (Vina active)\" vs \"docking: surrogate (no vina binary/receptor active right now)\"). | **UNCOMMITTED** |\n| `opensciencelab/tests.py` (~1624 lines, 76 tests) | **MODIFIED** \u2014 5 new tests appended: `test_vina_parse_output`, `test_vina_parse_garbage`, `test_vina_adapter_dock_end_to_end_with_fake_binary`, `test_vina_adapter_unavailable_returns_none`, `test_vina_objective_graceful_no_config`. Uses `tmp_path`, fake `vina` script on PATH, env var manipulation. | **UNCOMMITTED** |\n| `PHASE3.md` (~100 lines) | **NEW** \u2014 Phase 3 documentation: context, what was built, design decisions, verification output (76 passed, example runs with/without fake binary). | **UNCOMMITTED** |\n| `opensciencelab/preflight.py` (~360 lines) | Phase 2 item 4 deliverable. | **COMMITTED** (`34aa088`) |\n| `opensciencelab/tests.py` (pre-existing 71 tests) | All pass. | **COMMITTED** (`34aa088`) |\n| `scripts/materials_evolve_example.py` (~130 lines) | Phase 2 preflight integration. | **COMMITTED** (`34aa088`) |\n| `opensciencelab/cli.py` (~220 lines) | Phase 2 CLI extension. | **COMMITTED** (`34aa088`) |\n| `PHASE2.md` (~430 lines) | Phase 2 documentation. | **COMMITTED** (`34aa088`) |\n| `opensciencelab/services.py` (224 lines) | `default_services()`, `OptimizeService.evolve()`. READ ONLY. | Un", "working_state": "## Working state (extracted mechanically from tool records)\nFiles written/edited (most recent first):\n- /home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab/PHASE3.md\n- /home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab/opensciencelab/docking.py\nRecent shell commands:\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab && /usr/bin/python3 -m pytest -q opensciencelab/tests.py 2>&1 | grep -E \"passed|failed|error\" | tai  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab && git stash list | head -2; /usr/bin/python3 -m pytest -q opensciencelab/tests.py 2>&1 | grep -E \"  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab && git log --oneline -8 && git show --stat 34aa088 | tail -12  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab && /usr/bin/python3 -m pytest opensciencelab/tests.py --collect-only -q 2>&1 | grep \"::test_\" | tai  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab && ls *.md && /usr/bin/python3 -m pytest -q opensciencelab/tests.py 2>&1 | tail -1 && echo === A &&  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab && mkdir -p /tmp/p3vina && printf ''#!/usr/bin/env python3\\nprint(\"AutoDock Vina (fake)\")\\nprint(\"ex  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab && VINA_RECEPTOR_PDBQT=/tmp/p3vina/rec.pdbqt VINA_BINARY=/tmp/p3vina/vina /usr/bin/python3 scripts/  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab && VINA_RECEPTOR_PDBQT=/tmp/p3vina/rec.pdbqt VINA_BINARY=/tmp/p3vina/vina /usr/bin/python3 -c \" imp  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab && git status --short && git diff --stat && /usr/bin/python3 -m pytest -q opensciencelab/tests.py 2  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab && git diff base.py | head -60 && echo ====== && git diff PHASE2.md | head -40  [ok]\nTools used in the summarized span: ask_user, brain_recall, propose_plan, read_file, replace_in_file, run_shell, todo_write, write_file", "user_messages": ["Phase 2, item 4 only. Read PHASE2.md first (it records items 1\u20133, the defects found, and what is knowingly still broken). Item 3 (budget ledger) is ALREADY DONE and committed (see PHASE2.md: every evolve() call quotes predicted cost up front, is admitted/refused against remaining budget, and records cost/predicted_cost/delta_cost on the Bundle and in the manifest). Do not re-implement or \"fix\" it. Then implement the final open item from Phase 2 of openevolve_roadmap.md \u2014 **Pre-run checklist as a first-class `preflight()` API**: `preflight.py` exists, but today it plans around `structure/desig\u2026", "What is next to do?"], "user_messages_dropped": 0, "created_at": 1787514378.4659564, "model_used": "ollama:qwen3.8-27b:latest", "trimmed": false}');
INSERT INTO sessions VALUES('7362987f-a0e','/home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab','ollama:qwen3.8-27b:latest','auto','Phase 3 item 2 (the Vina adapter, 2529fa0) made a known Phas','builder',322,NULL,'[]',0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,'2026-08-23 23:05:16','{}','{"boundary_index": 199, "summary_text": "## Primary request and intent\n\nFix a known Phase 2 defect (documented in PHASE2.md lines 739\u2013744 under \"Still open\") that Phase 3 item 2 (Vina adapter, commit `2529fa0`) made live: the shipped domain evaluators in `drugdiscovery.py` and `materials.py` hardcode `tier=TIER_ZERO` on the `ScoreVector` they return. Because the ledger charges exactly what the `ScoreVector` declares, a real Vina dock is metered at tier-0 (0.01/eval) instead of the correct mid-tier rate, and PySCF (item 3, tier 2, 50/eval) would inherit the same hole.\n\n**Scope constraint (explicit, lasting):** The fix is in the **evaluator factories only**. Do NOT modify `base.py`, the ledger, `scoring.py`, `preflight`, or `manifest.py` \u2014 they already correctly charge what the vector declares, and a prior remediation (item 4) already made preflight re-quote mid-run tier changes.\n\n**Per-candidate tier decision rule (user-specified):** Use the same signal that already stamps `docking_method` as *real* vs *surrogate-offline*. Real docking \u2192 mid tier; surrogate \u2192 tier 0. Analogous rule for materials via `e_form_method` once CHGNet lands.\n\n**Verification requirement:** A mixed run (some candidates with real backend, some without) must show **two tiers** in `manifest budget.spent`, and preflight''s up-front quote must still refuse correctly.\n\n**Post-fix obligations:** Commit the fix by itself. Update PHASE2.md to mark the \"Still open\" entry as closed.\n\n## Key concepts and decisions\n\n- **Tier model** (in `base.py`): `TIER_ZERO` (0.01/eval, fast surrogate, **uncapped**), `TIER_ONE` (mid, real docking, cap 1000.0), `TIER_TWO` (50/eval, heavy like PySCF, cap 500.0). `budget_default()` returns `Budget(limits={1: 1000.0, 2: 500.0})`.\n- **ScoreVector** (in `base.py` L81): `.to_dict()` returns `{\"tier\": self.tier, \"metrics\": ...}`. The ledger charges what the vector says, so a wrong tier = wrong billing.\n- **Charging flow** \u2014 `adapters/optimize/adapter.py` L207\u2013221: calls `evaluator(cand)`, reads `t = int(getattr(vec, \"tier\", TIER_ZERO))`, charges `budget.admit(t, rate)`. The vector''s tier drives the charge.\n- **Design decision (resolve idiom):** Mirrors the `materials.py` pattern where `e_form_objective` owns a `resolve` function that returns `(score_value, stamp, tier)`. The evaluator calls `resolve` once per candidate and uses the returned tier for the `ScoreVector`. This avoids double-invoking the real backend. The assistant initially tried a separate `_docking_provenance` helper (too narrow) then restructured to match the materials idiom.\n- **`docking_objective` refactor:** Now returns `Tuple[Callable[[Candidate], float], Callable[[Candidate], str]]` where the score function carries a `.resolve` attribute that returns `(score, stamp, tier)`. `make_drug_evaluator` calls `docking_objective(docking_fn)[0]` and reads tier from the resolve result.\n- **`e_form_objective` refactor:** `resolve` extended to return `(value, stamp, tier)`. `make_materials_evaluator`''s `evaluate` pulls tier from this resolve call. Band-gap has no real backend yet (always surrogate \u2192 tier 0), so vector tier is e_form tier when scored, else tier 0.\n- **Preflight compatibility:** `_SENTINEL` (smi=\"CCO\") has no `docking_fn` \u2192 surrogate path \u2192 tier 0. Existing tests using `charged_tier=0` still pass because the sentinel produces tier 0.\n- **`scripts/drug_evolve_example.py:97`** and **`scripts/materials_evolve_example.py:86`**: Hardcode `charged_tier=0`. Out of scope (evaluator factory fix only).\n\n## Artifacts and files\n\nWorking directory: `/home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab`\n\n| File | Lines (current) | Role / Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| `opensciencelab/drugdiscovery.py` | **304** (was 282) | **FIXED.** Import now includes `TIER_ONE` (L37). `docking_objective` refactored to resolve-idiom returning score-fn with `.resolve` that yields `(score, stamp, tier)`. `make_drug_evaluator` uses `docking_objective(docking_fn)[0]` and reads tier from resolve. Verified by inline smoke and full test suite. |\n| `opensciencelab/materials.py` | **534** (was 528) | **FIXED.** Import updated to include `TIER_ONE` (L47). `e_form_objective` at L178 refactored: `resolve` now returns `(value, stamp, tier)`. `make_materials_evaluator`''s `evaluate` pulls tier from resolve. Verified by inline smoke and full test suite. |\n| `opensciencelab/docking.py` | 267 | Vina adapter. Stamps `docking_method` as `\"real\"` or `\"surrogate-offline\"`. Not modified. |\n| `opensciencelab/base.py` | 323 | Tier constants, `ScoreVector`, `Budget`, registry. Not modified. |\n| `opensciencelab/__init__.py` | \u2014 | Exports `TIER_ZERO`, `TIER_ONE`, `TIER_TWO` (lines 23\u201324). Not modified. |\n| `opensciencelab/preflight.py` | 696 | `_SENTINEL` (L99, smi=\"CCO\"), `_SENTINEL_MATERIAL` (L101). `_smoke_check` tier assertion at L656. Not modified. |\n| `opensciencelab/adapters/optimize/adapter.py` | 651 | `metered` logic L207\u2013221: charges at `vec.tier`. Not modified. |\n| `opensciencelab/tests.py` | 1655 | All 76 tests pass. Vina e2e test at L1569 uses fake binary with PDBQT and non-PDBQT candidates. `charged_tier=0` used throughout (still valid for sentinel). Tier assertions at L708\u2013742, L825\u2013838. Not modified. |\n| `scripts/drug_evolve_example.py` | \u2014 | L97: `charged_tier=0`. Out of scope. |\n| `scripts/materials_evolve_example.py` | \u2014 | L86: `charged_tier=0`. Out of scope. |\n| `PHASE2.md` | \u2014 | \"Still open\" entry at lines 739\u2013744. **Still needs to be marked closed.** |\n| `test_per_candidate_tier.py` | \u2014 | Temporary smoke test created then **deleted** (used for inline verification only). |\n\n## Errors and fixes\n\n1. **First patch to `drugdiscovery.py` was messy** \u2014 introduced \"garbage placeholder logic\" with a standalone `_docking_provenance` helper that was too narrow. Fixed by restructuring to the resolve idiom matching materials.py.\n\n2. **Redundant parallel implementations** \u2014 After the first cleanup, both a refactored `docking_objective` AND inlined logic existed in `make_drug_evaluator`. Fixed by making `make_drug_evaluator` call `docking_objective(docking_fn)[0]` and reading tier from `.resolve`.\n\n3. **`apply_patch` context mismatch** (one instance): \"Patch context does not match opensciencelab/drugdiscovery.py.\" Resolved by re-reading the file and using `replace_in_file` with exact old content instead.\n\n4. **`replace_in_file` found 0 replacements** for `materials.py` `evaluate` update: The old text didn''t match exactly. Resolved by re-reading the section (L360\u2013399) and providing a corrected old string.\n\n5. **User correction (implicit via design):** The assistant self-corrected the approach from a narrow `_docking_provenance` helper to the full resolve idiom to avoid double-invoking the backend and to match the existing materials pattern.\n\n## All user messages\n\n(No explicit user messages in this conversation segment \u2014 the assistant was continuing work from a prior session whose intent is captured in the compaction summary. The user''s instructions are embedded in the prior summary: fix evaluator factories only, use provenance signal for tier, verify two tiers in mixed run, commit, update PHASE2.md.)\n\n## Pending tasks\n\n1. **Add a proper regression test to `tests.py`** that demonstrates a mixed population (real + surrogate candidates) shows **two tiers** in `manifest budget.spent`. The assistant identified the Vina e2e test at L1569 as the pattern to follow (fake binary, PDBQT vs non-PDBQT candidates) and was reading the optimize adapter''s charging logic (L205\u2013234) to understand how to assert on `budget.spent` with two tier keys.\n2. **Commit the fix by itself** (drugdiscovery.py + materials.py changes).\n3. **Update PHASE2.md** lines 739\u2013744 to mark the \"Still open\" entry as closed.\n\n## Current work\n\nThe assistant had just:\n- Confirmed all 76 existing tests pass with the fix.\n- Read the optimize adapter''s `metered` charging code (L205\u2013234) to understand how `vec.tier` drives `budget.admit(t, rate)` and how `budget.spent` accumulates per-tier.\n- Read the Vina e2e test (L1569\u20131653) as a model for a fake-backend mixed-population test.\n- Was about to **write a new test in `tests.py`** that creates a mixed candidate population through the optimize adapter with a real docking_fn (some candidates) and surrogate (others), then asserts `budget.spent` has both tier-0 and tier-1 keys with correct amounts.\n\nThe drugdiscovery.py and materials.py fixes are functionally complete and verified. The test, commit, and PHASE2.md update remain.\n\n## Next step\n\nWrite a test in `opensciencelab/tests.py` (likely near the existing Vina e2e test at L1569 or the tier-assertion tests at L708\u2013742) that:\n1. Creates a `make_drug_evaluator` with a `docking_fn` that returns a float for some candidates", "working_state": "## Working state (extracted mechanically from tool records)\nFiles written/edited (most recent first):\n- test_per_candidate_tier.py\nRecent shell commands:\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab && grep -n \"TIER_ONE\\|TIER_ZERO\" opensciencelab/__init__.py opensciencelab/base.py | head -30  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab && grep -n \"make_drug_evaluator\\|make_materials_evaluator\\|docking_objective\\|e_form_objective\" ope  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab && grep -n \"tier\" opensciencelab/tests.py | head -60  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab && python -c \" import opensciencelab.drugdiscovery as d import opensciencelab.materials as m print(  [exit 127]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab && python3 -c \" import opensciencelab.drugdiscovery as d import opensciencelab.materials as m from   [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab && rm test_per_candidate_tier.py && grep -n \"_svc\\|def _svc\" opensciencelab/tests.py | head -5  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab && grep -rn \"charged_tier\" --include=\"*.py\" | head -30  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab && python3 -m pytest opensciencelab/tests.py -v 2>&1 | tail -80  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab && grep -n \"test_vina_adapter_dock_end_to_end_with_fake_binary\" opensciencelab/tests.py  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab && grep -n \"offline\\|hill\\|island\" opensciencelab/adapters/optimize/*.py | head -25  [ok]\nTools used in the summarized span: apply_patch, grep, read_file, replace_in_file, run_shell, write_file", "user_messages": ["Phase 3 item 2 (the Vina adapter, 2529fa0) made a known Phase 2 defect live. Fix it before any further Phase 3 adapter. The defect, named in PHASE2.md under \"Still open\": the shipped domain evaluators in drugdiscovery.py and materials.py hardcode tier=TIER_ZERO on the ScoreVector they return. The ledger charges what the ScoreVector says, so a real Vina dock \u2014 which docking.py now makes reachable \u2014 is metered as tier-0 at 0.01/eval instead of the mid-tier rate. PySCF (tier 2, 50/eval) in item 3 would inherit the same hole. Make the evaluator report the tier its backend actually ran at: real do\u2026"], "user_messages_dropped": 0, "created_at": 1787525084.913472, "model_used": "ollama:qwen3.8-27b:latest", "trimmed": false}');
INSERT INTO sessions VALUES('55b259f3-f8a','/home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab','ollama:qwen3.8-27b:latest','auto','Phase 3, item 1 — RDKit descriptor bank + the SMILES->PDBQT ','builder',231,NULL,'[]',0,0,NULL,NULL,'RDKit descriptor bank and PDBQT seam',0,'2026-08-24 06:37:21','{}','{"boundary_index": 179, "summary_text": "## Primary request and intent\n\nImplement **Phase 3, Item 1** of the OpenScienceLab roadmap: the **RDKit descriptor bank + SMILES\u21923D\u2192PDBQT seam**. This closes the single contract gap (`candidate.metadata[\"pdbqt_text\"]`) that has kept every candidate on the `_docking_surrogate` path and stamped `surrogate-offline`. The real path in `docking.py` (Vina adapter) has shipped but never executed for real.\n\n**Standing constraints (outlive these turns):**\n- RDKit must stay **optional** \u2014 every path must work with rdkit absent; surrogate stamps must be honest.\n- **Seed=1337** for conformer embedding (repo reproducibility pin).\n- **Tier honesty**: real RDKit descriptors are `TIER_ZERO` (the fast path); the PDBQT prep *makes* `TIER_ONE` docking reachable but is not itself tier-1.\n- **Do not touch** `ledger`, `base.py`, or `preflight` \u2014 they already charge what the `ScoreVector` declares.\n- No `vina` binary on this host \u2014 say plainly in the writeup that docking is not live.\n- Commit solo, write the item-1 section of `PHASE3.md`, and call `brain_note` against the OpenScienceLab thread for both the tier fix (8ae4493) and this item.\n\n## Key concepts and decisions\n\n- **`pdbqt_text` gap**: `docking.py`''s real path reads `candidate.metadata[\"pdbqt_text\"]`; nothing in the codebase fills it. The new `descriptors.py` module provides `populate_pdbqt(candidate, seed=1337)` that does SMILES \u2192 RDKit 3D embed \u2192 meeko PDBQT string.\n- **Descriptor bank**: `descriptors.py` exposes `descriptor_bank(smiles)` returning a dict of real RDKit-computed properties (QED, SA, MolWt, LogP, TPSA, HBA, HBD, RotBonds, AromaticRings, heavy_atoms, etc.), with graceful `None`/proxy fallback when RDKit is absent.\n- **SA_Score module relocation**: In rdkit 2026.03.5, the old path `rdkit.Chem.SA_Score.sascorer` is gone. The correct import is `from rdkit.Contrib.SA_Score import sascorer` and the function is `sascorer.calculateScore(mol)` (not `sascorer.sas(mol)`). The code must try both paths conditionally.\n- **Python scoping bug (critical)**: Assigning `Chem = None` / `AllChem = None` in an `except` block causes Python to mark those names as **local** throughout the entire function scope, making every earlier `try`-branch reference to them a `NameError`. The fix: never assign to those names in the `except` branch; rely solely on boolean flags (`_HAVE_RDKIT`, etc.).\n- **`Chem.GetNumHeavyAtoms` does not exist**: It is a method on the mol object (`mol.GetNumHeavyAtoms()`). Calling it on the module raised an exception that was swallowed by the `except` fallback, silently dropping all descriptors. Fixed to `mol.GetNumHeavyAtoms()`.\n- **Proxy pattern preserved**: `drugdiscovery.py`''s `qed_objective` / `sa_objective` try real RDKit first, fall back to `_qed_proxy` / `_sa_proxy` from `adapters/scoring.py`.\n- **In-place mutation**: `populate_pdbqt` must mutate `cand.metadata` in place (not rebind) to avoid losing external references.\n- **LogP is signed**: Ethanol has a slightly negative LogP (~0); test assertions must check finiteness, not non-negativity.\n- **Seam proof methodology**: Use a fake `vina` Python script on PATH that parses the config file and prints a valid Vina stdout table; confirm the adapter returns a float (real path) rather than `None` (surrogate fallback).\n- **Forced-off proof**: Use a `MetaPathFinder` blocker (`/tmp/nordk/block.py`) to raise `ImportError` for `rdkit` and `meeko` top-level imports, then run the suite and example script to confirm honest surrogate stamps.\n\n## Artifacts and files\n\n| Path | Role | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| `opensciencelab/descriptors.py` | **NEW** \u2014 RDKit descriptor bank + SMILES\u2192PDBQT seam. Contains `rdkit_available()`, `meeko_available()`, `descriptor_bank(smiles)`, `populate_pdbqt(cand, seed=1337)`, conditional imports of `rdkit`/`rdkit.Contrib.SA_Score`, `meeko`. 234 lines. | Created & finalized (all bugs fixed) |\n| `opensciencelab/drugdiscovery.py` | Drug-discovery evaluator. `_HAVE_RDKIT` sourced from `descriptors.rdkit_available()`; `qed_objective`/`sa_objective` try real RDKit then fall back to proxy; `_docking_from_metadata` reads `metadata[\"vina_score_kcal\"]`; evaluator notes include `\"meeko\"` key. | Modified |\n| `opensciencelab/adapters/scoring.py` | Proxy definitions (`_qed_proxy`, `_sa_proxy`) and tier constants. | Read (reference only, not modified) |\n| `opensciencelab/base.py` | `Candidate`, `ScoreVector`, `Bundle`, tier constants. | Read (constrained, not modified) |\n| `opensciencelab/docking.py` | Vina adapter (Phase 3 item 2). Reads `candidate.metadata[\"pdbqt_text\"]` for real path; shells to `vina` binary. | Read (267 lines, not modified) |\n| `scripts/drug_evolve_example.py` | Example script. Modified: when real Vina path is active, calls `descriptors.populate_pdbqt` on each candidate before dock; `charged_tier` declaration updated to tier-1 for real path. | Modified |\n| `scripts/materials_evolve_example.py` | Second example script. | Run clean (not modified) |\n| `opensciencelab/tests.py` | Test suite. New tests: `test_descriptor_bank_real_rdkit`, `test_populate_pdbqt_fills_metadata`, `test_forced_off_stays_on_the_stub_path`. LogP assertion fixed from `v >= 0.0` to finiteness check. 1902 lines. | Modified |\n| `PHASE3.md` | Phase roadmap. Item 2 (Vina adapter) recorded. **Item 1 section NOT yet written.** Line 187 shows `- [ ] **Item 1** \u2014 RD\u2026` (unresolved checkbox). | Read; write pending |\n| `/tmp/nordk/block.py` | MetaPathFinder blocker for forced-off tests. Blocking `rdkit` and `meeko` top-level imports. | Created (test utility) |\n| `/tmp/seamA/bin/vina` | Fake vina binary for seam proof. Parses `--config` file, prints valid Vina stdout table. | Created (test utility) |\n\n## Errors and fixes\n\n1. **Explorer tool `max_iterations_exceeded`** (from prior session): Abandoned tool, used targeted `read_file`/`grep`.\n\n2. **`rdkit.Chem.SA_Score` module missing in rdkit 2026.03.5**: The module moved to `rdkit.Contrib.SA_Score`. Additionally, the function name changed from `sascorer.sas(mol)` to `sascorer.calculateScore(mol)`. Fixed with conditional import trying `rdkit.Chem.SA_Score` first, then `rdkit.Contrib.SA_Score`, and calling `calculateScore`.\n\n3. **Python scoping bug \u2014 `except` branch assignments poison `try` branch**: Assigning `Chem = None` / `AllChem = None` in the `except` block made Python treat those names as function-local throughout the entire scope. Every `Chem.MolFromSmiles(...)` call in the `try` branch raised `NameError`, which was silently caught by the outer `except`. Fixed by removing all `= None` assignments from the `except` branch and relying solely on boolean flags.\n\n4. **`Chem.GetNumHeavyAtoms` does not exist**: Called as a module-level function but it''s a method on the mol object. The exception was swallowed by the broad `except`, causing the entire descriptor bank to silently fall back to proxies. Fixed to `mol.GetNumHeavyAtoms()`.\n\n5. **Test assertion `v >= 0.0` failed for LogP**: Ethanol has a slightly negative MolLogP. Fixed the test to assert finiteness (`math.isfinite`) rather than non-negativity.\n\n6. **Fake vina script syntax error**: Initial fake binary had a Python syntax error in the f-string/arg-parsing, causing it to crash. The adapter honestly returned `None`. Fixed the script; re-ran successfully.\n\n7. **`populate_pdbqt` rebind issue** (from prior session): Changed `cand.metadata = dict(md)` to in-place mutation `md[\"pdbqt_text\"] = pdbqt_str`.\n\n8. **Typo drift in test names** (from prior session): Multiple rewrites to fix corrupted identifiers.\n\n## All user messages\n\n1. **Full task briefing** (the only user message, from prior session): Phase 3 item 1 \u2014 RDKit descriptor bank + SMILES\u2192PDBQT seam. Read PHASE3.md first; HEAD 8ae4493, 78 tests green; the `pdbqt_text` gap is the whole point; environment verified (rdkit 2026.03.5, meeko 0.7.1, scipy 1.18.1, gemmi 0.7.5 in ~/.local); no vina binary; constraints (RDKit optional, seed=1337, tier honesty TIER_ZERO, don''t touch ledger/base/preflight); verification requirements (full suite + both example scripts + show a candidate with `pdbqt_text` and the Vina adapter taking its real path on the fake binary + rdkit-off run must pass with surrogate stamp); post-work (commit solo, PHASE3.md item-1 section, `brain_note` for tier fix 8ae4493 and this item).\n\n## Pending tasks\n\n- **Write the item-1 section in `PHASE3.md`**: Document what was built, the SA_Score relocation, the scoping bug lesson, proof results (85 tests green, seam verified, forced-off verified), and the plain statement that dock", "working_state": "## Working state (extracted mechanically from tool records)\nRecent shell commands:\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab && ls scripts/ && /usr/bin/python3 -m scripts.materials_evolve_example 2>&1 | tail -15  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab && /usr/bin/python3 - <<''PY'' import os, stat, subprocess, sys, tempfile from pathlib import Path tm  [exit 1]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab && /usr/bin/python3 - <<''PY'' import os, tempfile from pathlib import Path tmp = Path(tempfile.mkdte  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab && rm -rf /tmp/seamA && mkdir -p /tmp/seamA/bin && cat > /tmp/seamA/bin/vina <<''EOF'' #!/usr/bin/env  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab && PATH=/tmp/seamA/bin:$PATH VINA_RECEPTOR_PDBQT=/tmp/seamA/rec.pdbqt VINA_BINARY=vina /usr/bin/pyt  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab && head -c 900 /tmp/seamA/runs/run-f13faa57/scored.jsonl; echo; echo ---; python3 -c \" import json   [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab && mkdir -p /tmp/nordk && cat > /tmp/nordk/block.py <<''EOF'' import importlib.abc, sys class _Blocke  [ok]\n- cd /home/ionbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab 2>/dev/null || cd /home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab cat > /tmp/nordk/block_e  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab && /usr/bin/python3 -m pytest -q opensciencelab/tests.py 2>&1 | tail -2 && PYTHONPATH=/tmp/nordk /u  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab && grep -n \"item 1\\|item-1\\|Item 1\" PHASE3.md | head; echo ---; tail -30 PHASE3.md; echo ---; git s  [ok]\nTools used in the summarized span: grep, read_file, replace_in_file, run_shell, todo_write", "user_messages": ["Phase 3, item 1 \u2014 RDKit descriptor bank + the SMILES->PDBQT seam. Read PHASE3.md first (it records item 2, the Vina adapter, and the item-2 follow-up that made the evaluators bill at the tier they actually ran at). HEAD is 8ae4493, tree is clean, 78 tests green. ## What this item is for `docking.py` shipped a real AutoDock Vina adapter, and it has never once taken its real path in a run. The reason is one line of its contract: it needs `candidate.metadata[\"pdbqt_text\"]`, and NOTHING in the codebase fills that. Every candidate falls to `_docking_surrogate` and is stamped `surrogate-offline`. I\u2026"], "user_messages_dropped": 0, "created_at": 1787553005.552123, "model_used": "ollama:qwen3.8-27b:latest", "trimmed": false}');
