INSERT INTO sessions VALUES('12e1fa55-72b','/home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab','ollama:qwen3.8-27b:latest','auto','Phase 3, item 3 — the PySCF DFT adapter (the tier-2 path).','builder',329,NULL,'[]',0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,'2026-08-24 19:24:26','{}','{"boundary_index": 229, "summary_text": "# Compaction Summary\n\n## 1. Primary request and intent\n\nBuild Phase 3, item 3 of the OpenScienceLab roadmap: a **PySCF DFT adapter** (tier-2 scoring path) for small molecules, gated to top-N candidates only. Standing constraints (inherited, still in force):\n\n- **Never raise mid-evolve** \u2014 every failure mode (missing pyscf, SCF non-convergence, too many atoms, timeout, bad geometry) degrades to `None` so the caller falls back to the stamped surrogate. A non-converged SCF must NOT be returned as a real number.\n- **Top-N gate is the point of this item** \u2014 DFT must NOT run on every candidate in the inner loop. The gate must be testable and bound DFT calls.\n- **Reuse the conformer** from `descriptors.py` (one embedding, two consumers). Do NOT write a second embedding path.\n- **Match the idiom** of `docking.py` (item 2) and `descriptors.py` (item 1) \u2014 same config/availability/no-raise shape.\n- **Tier contract (8ae4493):** `resolve(cand)` \u2192 `(value, provenance, tier)`, resolved ONCE per candidate. Return `TIER_TWO` for real DFT, `TIER_ZERO` for surrogate. Do NOT hardcode a tier.\n- **Do NOT modify** `base.py`, `preflight.py`, or the budget ledger.\n- **Keep 85 tests passing** (floor) \u2014 now 92 pass.\n- **Environment constraint:** always run tests as `/usr/bin/python3 -m pytest opensciencelab/tests.py -q` (Python 3.14 under `/usr/bin/python3`). Bare `python3` is miniforge 3.13 with none of the needed packages.\n- PySCF, RDKit, meeko, scipy, gemmi are under `/usr/bin/python3` ONLY. torch, chgnet are NOT installed and must not be pulled in.\n- No `vina` binary on this host.\n- Fix the stale PHASE3.md header (line 9), record item 3, write a brain_note, document in PHASE3.md, then commit.\n\n## 2. Key concepts and decisions\n\n- **Three-tier scoring architecture:** TIER_ZERO = bundled surrogate/proxy; TIER_ONE = Vina docking (item 2); TIER_TWO = PySCF DFT (this item). The ledger charges whatever tier the ScoreVector declares.\n- **Higher-is-better sign convention:** HOMO-LUMO gap in eV is the natural tier-2 observable (bigger gap = more stable).\n- **Verified PySCF API (measured):** `gto.M` \u2192 `dft.RKS` \u2192 `mf.xc = \"b3lyp\"` \u2192 `mf.kernel()`. Check `mf.converged` (bool). HOMO = `mf.mo_energy[mf.mo_occ > 0].max()`, LUMO = `mf.mo_energy[mf.mo_occ == 0].min()`, gap_eV = `(lumo - homo) * 27.2114`.\n- **Basis-set matters:** Water gap \u2248 9.67 eV with 6-31g* (spec anchor), \u2248 13.33 eV with sto-3g. Tests use 6-31g* to match the spec''s 9.5\u201310.0 band.\n- **PySCF `spin` parameter = Nalpha \u2212 Nbeta** (NOT 2S+1). Water (10 e\u207b, closed-shell) needs `spin=0`. Default corrected from 1 to 0.\n- **`pyscf.dft.RKS` is a factory function** (returns a class via `get_class()`), NOT a class itself. To patch for non-converged tests, monkeypatch `pyscf.dft.RKS` to a fake factory function returning a FakeMf with `converged=False`.\n- **Optional-dependency pattern:** flag-based import via `_HAVE_PYSCF` boolean, NO `= None` shadowing. `pyscf_available()` mirrors `rdkit_available()` (it''s a **module-level function**, not a method on the adapter).\n- **Config object:** `DFTConfig` dataclass (basis, xc, charge, spin, max_atoms, timeout, top_n) with `_config_from_env()` helper mirroring `VinaConfig`/`_config_from_env()` in docking.py.\n- **Top-N gate design:** Per-instance call counter (`self.calls`) on `DFTAdapter`. If `self.calls >= self.config.top_n`, `score()` returns `None` immediately. Simple, testable, no heapq.\n- **Conformer reuse:** `descriptors.py._conform_3d(smi)` returns list of `(symbol, x, y, z)` tuples. DFT adapter calls this same helper.\n- **`dft_objective` factory lives in `drugdiscovery.py`** (mirrors `docking_objective`), NOT in `dft.py`. The dft.py module contains the adapter, config, and pure-kernel helper only. This keeps the evaluator''s import path uniform.\n- **Wiring:** `dft` is **opt-in** \u2014 NOT in the default `OBJECTIVES = (\"docking\", \"qed\", \"sa\")`. A caller adds `\"dft\"` to the `objectives` tuple and optionally passes a `dft_adapter=` to `make_drug_evaluator` / `drug_evolve`. Tier = max of dock/dft per candidate.\n- **`_gap_surrogate`**: deterministic proxy (crude size/unsaturation trend) returned when DFT is unavailable or gate blocks, stamped TIER_ZERO.\n\n## 3. Artifacts and files\n\n| Path | Role | Status |\n|------|------|--------|\n| `opensciencelab/dft.py` (~413 lines) | **New file** \u2014 PySCF DFT adapter. Contains: `DFTConfig` dataclass, `pyscf_available()` (module-level fn), `_HAVE_PYSCF` flag, `_atom_block()`, `_run_rks(atoms, cfg)` (pure kernel, raises on non-converged), `DFTAdapter` class (per-instance `self.calls` top-N gate, `score(cand)` \u2192 `Optional[float]`, no-raise), `_config_from_env()`. **Does NOT contain `dft_objective`** (lives in drugdiscovery). | **Complete, 92 tests pass** |\n| `opensciencelab/drugdiscovery.py` (~409 lines) | Evaluator + factories. **Modified:** added `from . import dft as _dft`, `TIER_TWO` import, `dft_objective` factory (mirrors `docking_objective`, returns `(score_fn, method_fn)` with `resolve` protocol), `_gap_surrogate`, `dft_adapter` param on `make_drug_evaluator` and `drug_evolve`, weights dict updated with `\"dft\": 1.0`, `__all__` updated. OBJECTIVES comment clarifies \"dft\" is opt-in. | **Modified, verified** |\n| `opensciencelab/tests.py` (~2082 lines) | Full test suite. **7 new DFT tests** added after the item-2 tests (around L1848+): `test_dft_h2o_gap_in_expected_band`, `test_dft_gap_is_monotonic_heavy_atom`, `test_dft_top_n_gate_blocks_and_returns_none`, `test_dft_non_converged_returns_none`, `test_dft_pyscf_absent_degrades_cleanly`, `test_dft_objective_real_path_and_stamp`, `test_dft_objective_surrogate_when_gated`. Helper `_gap(smi, basis=\"6-31g*\")` replaces earlier `_run(smi)`. | **Modified, 92 tests all pass** |\n| `opensciencelab/descriptors.py` (282 lines) | Item 1: RDKit descriptors + SMILES\u2192PDBQT. Contains `_conform_3d(smi)` helper. | Unchanged |\n| `opensciencelab/docking.py` (267 lines) | Item 2: Vina adapter. Contains `docking_objective`, `_config_from_env`, `VinaAdapter`. | Unchanged (idiom reference) |\n| `opensciencelab/base.py` (323 lines) | Tier constants, ScoreVector, ledger. | DO NOT MODIFY |\n| `opensciencelab/__init__.py` (72 lines) | Package init. | Unchanged |\n| `PHASE3.md` (309 lines) | Phase 3 documentation. **Stale header at line 9 still unfixed. Item 3 not yet recorded.** | **Pending update** |\n| `scripts/drug_evolve_example.py` (159 lines) | Drug evolution example script. | Unchanged |\n| `../openevolve_roadmap.md` | Roadmap: line 101 = PySCF DFT item. | Unchanged |\n\n## 4. Errors and fixes\n\n1. **Accidentally dropped `_docking_surrogate`** when editing drugdiscovery.py \u2014 `docking_objective` still referenced it. Fixed by re-inserting the function.\n2. **H2O gap test used wrong basis:** Test used sto-3g (gap \u2248 13.33 eV) but expected 9.5\u201310.0 band. Fixed by switching test helper `_run(smi)` \u2192 `_gap(smi, basis=\"6-31g*\")` (gap \u2248 9.67 eV, matching spec anchor).\n3. **Non-converged test couldn''t patch `pyscf.dft.RKS`:** Discovered `RKS` is a factory function (not a class). Fixed test to monkeypatch `pyscf.dft.RKS` with a fake factory returning a FakeMf with `converged=False`.\n4. **Pyscf-absent test called `a.available()`:** `pyscf_available()` is a module-level function, not a method on DFTAdapter. Fixed test to use `pyscf_available()` or monkeypatch `_HAVE_PYSCF`.\n5. **Broken stub `test_dft_gap_is_real_and_homonotonic`** with dead code left in tests.py \u2014 removed.\n6. **Duplicate `dft_objective` in dft.py:** The factory was initially written in dft.py, then also needed in drugdiscovery.py. Resolved by removing it from dft.py (canonical location is drugdiscovery.py, mirroring `docking_objective`). Updated the comment block", "working_state": "## Working state (extracted mechanically from tool records)\nRecent shell commands:\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab && grep -n \"from . import dft\\|from . import\\|import dft\\|_dft\\.\\|import dft\" opensciencelab/drugdi  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab && grep -n \"dft_objective\" opensciencelab/tests.py scripts/ opensciencelab/PHASE3.md 2>/dev/null  [exit 2]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab && /usr/bin/python3 -c \" import opensciencelab.dft as d from opensciencelab.descriptors import _con  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab && grep -n \"_run(\" opensciencelab/tests.py  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab && /usr/bin/python3 -c \" from pyscf import dft import inspect print(''RKS type:'', type(dft.RKS)) pri  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab && /usr/bin/python3 -c \" import opensciencelab.dft as d class FakeMf: def __init__(self, mol): self  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab && /usr/bin/python3 -m pytest opensciencelab/tests.py::test_dft_pyscf_absent_degrades_cleanly -x 2>  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab && /usr/bin/python3 -m pytest opensciencelab/tests.py -q 2>&1 | tail -8  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab && grep -n \"dft_objective\" opensciencelab/__init__.py opensciencelab/dft.py opensciencelab/drugdisc  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab && grep -rn \"_config_from_env\" opensciencelab/ scripts/ 2>/dev/null  [ok]\nTools used in the summarized span: grep, read_file, replace_in_file, run_shell, todo_write", "user_messages": ["Phase 3, item 3 \u2014 the PySCF DFT adapter (the tier-2 path). Baseline: commit 6f71a30 on branch phase2-drug-and-materials. 85 tests pass. Item 1 (RDKit descriptors + SMILES->PDBQT) and item 2 (Vina adapter) are done. Item 3 is the roadmap''s \"PySCF adapter for DFT on small molecules (top-candidates only)\" (openevolve_roadmap.md:101), and its cost rule is line 168: \"keep DFT/Vina on top-N\". ENVIRONMENT \u2014 already verified for you, do not spend context rediscovering it: * PySCF 2.14.0 IS INSTALLED, but only for /usr/bin/python3 (Python 3.14). `python3` on PATH is miniforge 3.13 and has NO pytest, N\u2026"], "user_messages_dropped": 0, "created_at": 1787598578.5952845, "model_used": "ollama:qwen3.8-27b:latest", "trimmed": false}');
