INSERT INTO sessions VALUES('6ac5ea43-b0c','/home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab','ollama:qwen3.8-27b:latest','auto','You are building OpenScienceLab, an open-source, Claude-Scie','builder',368,NULL,'[]',0,0,NULL,NULL,'OpenScienceLab Live Kernel Verification',0,'2026-08-25 18:07:17','{}','{"boundary_index": 285, "summary_text": "# Compaction Summary \u2014 OpenScienceLab Phase-3 Live Kernel Verification\n\n## 1. Primary request and intent\n\nBuild **OpenScienceLab**, an open-source Claude-Science-class stack combining OpenEvolve (evolutionary optimization) with drug-discovery + materials-science scoring. Repo: `~/opensciencelab` (full path: `/home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab`), branch `phase2-drug-and-materials`.\n\n**Three ordered tasks (in priority order):**\n\n1. **Step 1 \u2014 Live kernel verification:** All four Phase-3 adapters (Vina docking, RDKit/meeko descriptors, PySCF DFT, CHGNet E_form) are proven only by fake-kernel tests. Prove the REAL paths execute and produce the same contract behavior (ScoreVector sign, tier stamp, budget charge) on a host where the binaries exist. Deliverables: a verification Docker image with all four kernels, a `scripts/live_verify.py` that runs fixed candidates through each adapter''s real path and compares against test fixtures, a `runs/<id>/` manifest, and a CI job or documented `docker-run.sh verify` path. **Exit gate:** green log, every adapter row un-stamped (real) for \u22651 candidate, budget charges at declared tier, failed-kernel still degrades without raising.\n\n2. **Step 2 \u2014 Phase 4: canonical report shape + kill criteria:** Reconcile `report.py` to the roadmap''s five sections. Add fragility derivation, repro command emission. Confirm plateau-stop and budget-pause are reachable. Exit gate: a non-expert can read one rendered report, name top-3, state why, and copy-paste a re-run command.\n\n3. **Step 3 \u2014 Pick two canonical targets (ASK, don''t assume):** Present drug target (HCV NS3/4A vs KRAS G12D) and materials target (perovskite solar absorbers vs battery cathodes) to the user. Do NOT build either until the user answers.\n\n**Standing constraints (violation = reject):**\n- Provenance first-class: every run lands in `runs/<id>/` with a manifest.\n- Honesty stamps load-bearing: proxy-scored items MUST stay stamped (`surrogate-offline`); never let a real-path stamp appear on a proxy number; never remove degrade-to-None adapters.\n- No-raise adapter boundary: kernels fail with sentinels (`_DFTUnavailable`, `_ChgNetUnavailable`); adapters degrade to None.\n- One entry point (`OptimizeService.evolve`), one budget ledger (quote \u2192 admit \u2192 charge at `ScoreVector.tier`). Do not fork a second billing path.\n- Test suite must end green: baseline 97 tests (`python3 -m pytest -q opensciencelab/tests.py`). Record count before/after each step.\n- Commit after each step with the step name; update matching PHASE*.md progress line. Don''t bundle steps in one commit.\n- Out of scope: Phase 2 behavior, Phase 3 adapter contracts (tier semantics, no-raise boundary, top-N gates), registry names, manifest schema version.\n- No new dependencies on the shipped path without listing them in pyproject.toml extras and the Dockerfile.\n\n## 2. Key concepts and decisions\n\n- **ScoreVector contract:** Each adapter returns a `ScoreVector` with `metrics` (dict of values), `notes` (stamps like `method: \"surrogate-offline\"`), and `tier` (int: 0=free descriptors, 1=docking/CHGNet, 2=DFT/PySCF). Budget is charged at `tier`.\n- **Tier semantics:** TIER_ZERO (descriptors, no binary needed), TIER_ONE (Vina docking, CHGNet), TIER_TWO (PySCF DFT). Higher tier = more compute.\n- **No-raise adapter pattern:** Real kernels can be absent. Adapters catch `_DFTUnavailable`, `_ChgNetUnavailable` sentinels and degrade to `None` scores rather than raising. This is load-bearing.\n- **Honesty stamps:** Proxy/offline scoring MUST be stamped (e.g., `\"surrogate-offline\"`). Real-path scoring should be UNSTAMPED (no surrogate stamp). This distinction is the core verification criterion for Step 1.\n- **Registry pattern:** `opensciencelab.base.registry` holds adapter instances. `OptimizeService` is the single entry point.\n- **Verification image decisions (from prior session, still relevant):**\n  - Python 3.11 base image (confirmed cp311 wheels exist).\n  - Vina binary: v1.2.5 from GitHub releases, sha256 `fa0126a28a9ea9162d1b161dfa92bc76e632416db28ca246278ea4b2dc6860cb`.\n  - Receptor: generated programmatically via meeko \u2192 strip flexible-ligand blocks \u2192 rigid receptor.\n  - Package pins: `rdkit==2024.3.5`, `meeko==0.5.0`, `pyscf==2.5.0`, `torch==2.4.1+cpu`, `torchvision==0.19.1+cpu`, `chgnet` (valid version), `pymatgen` (valid version). CPU-only torch.\n  - No `.github/` CI directory exists yet; path is `docker/docker-run.sh verify`.\n- **Budget/manifest API (confirmed this session):**\n  - `Budget` (manifest.py): `costs` maps tier\u2192units/candidate; `limits` dict; `spent` dict (default `{0:0,1:0,2:0}`); `spend(tier, units)` raises on negative or over-limit; `admit(costs)` is the all-or-nothing gate; `spend_all(dict)` exists.\n  - `RunDirectory` / `Manifest` classes in manifest.py (419 lines) for `runs/<id>/` persistence.\n  - `Manifest.record` signature (line ~280): takes `adapter_name`, `candidate_id`, `score`, `artifacts`, `predicted_cost`, `delta_cost`, `budget_exceeded`; hashes a canonical summary of the call.\n  - `Manifest.record_error(message)` appends timestamped error string.\n  - `OptimizeService.evolve` in services.py is the single entry point that owns Budget, pulls adapter from registry, calls `Adapter.run()`.\n- **Adapter constructor signatures (confirmed this session):**\n  - `VinaAdapter(config=...)` \u2014 parameter is `config`, NOT `cfg`.\n  - `ChgNetAdapter(config=...)` \u2014 parameter is `config`. Has `top_n` and `relax` kwargs on `ChgNetConfig`.\n- **Adapter score methods confirmed:**\n  - `docking.py`: `VinaAdapter.score(cand)` \u2192 checks `available()`, reads `cand.metadata[\"pdbqt_text\"]`, invokes vina binary via subprocess, parses stdout with `_parse_vina_output`, returns `ScoreVector` with tier=1. Helper: `_best_affinity`.\n  - `dft.py`: `DFTAdapter` at line 209 (410-line file). Checks `_HAVE_PYSCF` flag, runs PySCF SCF, returns `ScoreVector` tier=2 or raises `_DFTUnavailable`. Helper `_gap(smi, basis)` does one SCF.\n  - `chgnet.py`: `ChgNetAdapter.score(cand)` \u2192 builds 2-atom prototype cell from cation/anion metadata, runs CHGNet, returns native-sign E_form (eV/f.u.) or None. Tier=1.\n  - `descriptors.py`: `compute_descriptors(smi)` \u2192 RDKit/mol, returns dict of qed/sa/mollogp/tpsa etc. Also `descriptor_bank(smi)` returns a dict. Tier=0.\n- **Drug evaluator wiring:** `drugdiscovery.py` (409 lines) `make_drug_evaluator(docking_fn=...)` \u2192 when docking_fn is None, all objectives stamped `method: \"surrogate-offline\"`. When docking_fn supplies real PDBQT, the docking score is unstamped.\n- **Materials evaluator wiring:** `materials.py` (537 lines) `make_materials_evaluator(chgnet_fn=...)` \u2192 when chgnet_fn returns None, falls back to stamped surrogate. Resolution order in `e_form_objective` (line 178): pre-scored metadata (real) \u2192 `chgnet_fn` (real) \u2192 composition surrogate (stamped `surrogate-offline`). Native-sign E_form (negative=stable), ScoreVector requires \"higher is better\" so sign is inverted.\n- **`descriptors.py` meeko API:** Uses `MoleculePreparation` (NOT `MoleculePrepOptions`), `PDBQTWriterLegacy.write_string`. Requires 3D conformer + Hs before `prepare()`.\n\n### CRITICAL BUG DISCOVERED THIS SESSION (Step 1''s core finding):\n\n**`opensciencelab/docking.py` \u2014 `_parse_vina_output` (around lines 95\u2013118) looks for a literal `\"exhaustive docking\"` header that real AutoDock Vina 1.2.x NEVER outputs.** Real vina 1.2.5 stdout is a simple tab-separated table like:\n```\nmode|affinity|rmsd_l|rmsd_b\n     1       -7.2     0.000   0.000\n```\nThe parser expects a multi-line \"exhaustive docking\" output format that only exists in the fake-kernel test fixtures. **Result: on any real host, `VinaAdapter.score()` always silently returns None (degraded), even when the binary and receptor are perfectly valid.** This is the exact fake-vs-real gap Step 1 exists to catch. The fix must:\n- Accept real vina 1.2.x stdout (the simple mode/affinity table)\n- Continue to accept the fake fixture format (so existing 97 tests stay green)\n- The fix is in `docking.py`, NOT in `live_verify.py` \u2014 it''s a genuine adapter contract bug.\n\n**`scripts/live_verify.py` was corrupted during a re-slice operation** (file went from 414 \u2192 314 lines). The `_row_chgnet` (G3) and `_row_dft` (G4) helper functions were **lost** and need to be restored.", "working_state": "## Working state (extracted mechanically from tool records)\nFiles written/edited (most recent first):\n- /tmp/_patch_liveverify.py\nRecent shell commands:\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab && python3 - <<''PYEOF'' p = \"scripts/live_verify.py\" src = open(p).read() start = src.index(\"def _ro  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab && PYTHONPATH=. VINA_BINARY=/tmp/vinabin/vina VINA_RECEPTOR_PDBQT=/tmp/receptor.pdbqt VINA_EXHAUSTI  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab && PYTHONPATH=. VINA_BINARY=/tmp/vinabin/vina VINA_RECEPTOR_PDBQT=/tmp/receptor.pdbqt VINA_EXHAUSTI  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab && sed -n ''1,60p'' opensciencelab/docking.py && grep -n \"_best_affinity\\|VINA RESULT\" opensciencelab  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab && grep -n \"CHGNet\\|_ChgNetUnavailable\\|class ChgNetAdapter\\|def __init__\\|def score\\|def chgnet\\|_  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab && grep -n \"exhaustive docking\" opensciencelab/*.py scripts/*.py && sed -n ''1530,1600p'' openscience  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab && sed -n ''2040,2090p'' opensciencelab/tests.py  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab && grep -n \"class DFTAdapter\\|def score\\|def gap\\|class DFTConfig\\|def __init__\\|_HAVE_PYSCF\\|_DFTU  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab && grep -n \"docking_method\\|def docking_objective\\|surrogate-offline\\|def e_form_objective\\|chgnet_  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab && grep -n \"def rate\\|def spend_all\\|def record\\|def to_dict\\|def save\\|class Manifest\\|class Budge  [ok]\nTools used in the summarized span: read_file, replace_in_file, run_shell, todo_write, write_file", "user_messages": ["You are building OpenScienceLab, an open-source, Claude-Science-class stack combining OpenEvolve (evolutionary optimization) with drug discovery + materials science scoring. Repo: ~/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab, branch phase2-drug-and-materials. == READ FIRST (in this order) == 1. openevolve_roadmap.md (north star, definitions of done) 2. opensciencelab/PHASE2.md (Phase 2 \u2014 CLOSED, do not re-do) 3. opensciencelab/PHASE3.md (Phase 3 \u2014 CLOSED in code, read the honesty caveats) 4. opensciencelab/opensciencelab/{base,drugdiscovery,materials,docking,dft,chgnet,descriptors,preflight,report}.\u2026"], "user_messages_dropped": 0, "created_at": 1787679910.4430785, "model_used": "ollama:qwen3.8-27b:latest", "trimmed": false}');
