 So confirmed: no files have been modified.\n\nNow, let me note the key decisions made in the new content that OVERRIDE the previous summary:\n\n1. **Crypto fix**: The coworker decided on \"Option B\" \u2014 JWK reconstruction via `createPrivateKey`/`createPublicKey` with `format: ''jwk''` \u2014 NOT DER reconstruction. This is a correction from the previous summary.\n\nLet me look at the actual decision text:\n- \"My probe''s `.bind` was wrong\" (earlier confusion)\n- \"`privRaw` came out 0 bytes \u2014 so `export({format:''jwk''}).d` is not where Ed25519 private material lives\" \u2014 but then they realized\n- \"`createPrivateKey` works fine with a JWK \u2014 so `fromJwk` can work via native JWK parsing. My earlier ''fromB64url + DER reconstruction'' path was over-engineered and wrong\"\n- \"Option B (JWK via createPrivateKey/createPublicKey with format:\"jwk\") is clean, valid, and needs no hex constants \u2014 my fix choice.\"\n- \"JWK-method round-trips and rejects tampering. I now have everything for the crypto fix.\"\n\nSo the decision is clearly Option B now.\n\n2. **Budget fix**: `>=` operator change in checkBucket. Let me look at the exact context.\n\nThe engine.ts checkBucket returns `remaining < 0` \u2192 something, `remaining < priceMicros` \u2192 limit exceeded error, else OK.\n\nThe coworker mentions \"my `>=` operator fix\". So the current code uses `<` and they''re changing to `>=`. This is the exact-fit boundary fix.\n\n3. **globMatch fix**: The \"apex\" candidate \u2014 leading dot of split part becomes optional. `*.news.example.com/*` matches apex host. This passes both assertions A1 and A2.\n\nWait, let me re-read. The coworker''s probes were about globMatch. The \"apex\" function:\n```js\nfunction apexRe(p){\n const parts = p.split(\"*\").map(esc).map(e => e.replace(/^\\./,\"(?:\\.)?\"));\n return new RegExp(\"^{0}$\", parts.join(\".*\"));\n}\n```\nThis makes the leading dot optional. So `*.news.example.com/*` becomes `(?:\\.)?news\\.example\\.com` matching both `.news.example.com` and `news.example.com`. This passes A1 (apex host matches) and A2 (rejects other host).\n\nActually, wait. Let me look at the actual assertion. From the previous summary, the glob tests were about matching `*.news.example.com/*`. The \"apex\" candidate passes both glob assertions.\n\n4. **dashboard join fix**: `\"-\".join` bug at line 41 in dashboard.ts. TS2339, join on string. Need to fix.\n\n5. **license-id derivation**: `slugFromUrl` returns `new URL(url).href` (full URL) instead of pathname. Test expects `/r/73`. Fix: return pathname.\n\nNow let me look at the budget test contradiction more carefully. The previous summary mentioned:\n- Test line 22-33: \"blocks once the hourly tenant ceiling is consumed\"\n- Test line 59-64: \"line-item daily\"\n\nThe coworker in the new content reads engine.test.ts 30-61 and 59-73, and engine.ts. Let me see what they concluded about the fix.\n\nThe mention of \"my `>=` operator fix\" and \"confirm the gateway tests don''t rely on `>`-style exact-fit (which my `>=` operator fix would change)\" suggests the fix is changing a comparison operator.\n\nActually, I realize I should focus on what''s concretely established. Let me note:\n\nThe budget fix is a `>=` operator change in the engine''s checkBucket (exact-fit boundary). But there was a concern about whether changing it breaks gateway tests that use `>`-style exact-fit.\n\nHmm, but actually the previous summary flagged a genuine contradiction: the hourly ceiling test at line 32 expects a throw after 1000\u00b5s against a 2000\u00b5s ceiling, and the line-item test expects /line-item daily/. Let me not over-claim the contradiction is resolved. The coworker is still verifying.\n\nActually, wait. Let me re-read the last assistant message and tool calls. The coworker''s last actions were:\n- \"All four packages are now fully diagnosed. Let me do two final safety checks before editing\"\n- Check 1: gateway tests don''t rely on `>`-style exact-fit\n- Check 2: JsonWebKey valid type\n\nAnd the very last tool call was a JWK parse test on the active node (cut off).\n\nSo the coworker is about to start editing. No files edited yet.\n\nLet me also capture the specifics of each bug:\n\n**Bug 1: crypto fromJwk (identity/ring.ts)**\n- 5 sites: lines 159, 174, 269, 280, 299 use `KeyObject.fromJwk(...)`\n- Also `JsonWebKey` used as a type at lines 75, 76\n- Fix: replace `KeyObject.fromJwk(...)` with `createPrivateKey`/`createPublicKey` using JWK\n- Key material: `privateRaw` = JWK `d`, `publicRaw` = JWK `x`, both base64url strings\n\nLet me look at the exact ring.ts content to capture the relevant code. From the reads:\n- Line 1: `import { KeyObject, generateKeyPairSync, sign, verify } from ''node:crypto'';`\n- Line 60: `export class KeyRing {`\n- Line 75-76: `const pubJwk = publicKey.export({ format: ''jwk'' }) as JsonWebKey; const privJwk = ...`\n- Line 120-122: `now = Date.parse(this.clock.now()); return this.all().filter(...)`\n- Line 159, 174: fromJwk sites (sign/verify)\n- Line 241+: `static parse(token: string)` PACT parsing\n- Lines 269, 280, 299: fromJwk sites\n\nI need to see the actual sign/verify code at 159-174 to capture the fix. But I don''t have that exact content. Let me note the sites and the decision.\n\nActually, I have read_file results for:\n- ring.ts 1-60 (lines 1-60)\n- ring.ts 60-119 (lines 60-119)\n- ring.ts 120-239 (lines 120-239)\n- ring.ts 240-323 (lines 240-323)\n\nThe fromJwk sites 159, 174 are in the 120-239 range, which I don''t have the full content of. So I''ll note the sites and the fix approach without the exact code.\n\n**Bug 2: globMatch (budget/policy.ts)**\n- Current impl fails A1 (`*.news.example.com/*` should match apex host)\n- Fix: \"apex\" candidate \u2014 make leading dot optional in the split parts\n\n**Bug 3: dashboard.join (audit/dashboard.ts)**\n- Line 41: `\"-\".join` \u2014 string has no join method\n- Fix: need to see actual code. From dashboard reads (1-45), I have the header but not line 41. Note the bug location.\n\n**Bug 4: budget engine exact-fit (budget/engine.ts)**\n- checkBucket uses `remaining < priceMicros` / `remaining < 0`\n- Fix: `>=` operator change\n- Concern: gateway tests don''t rely on `>`-style exact-fit\n\n**Bug 5: license-id derivation (license/engine.ts)**\n- `slugFromUrl` returns `new URL(url).href` (full URL) instead of pathname\n- Test expects `/r/73`\n- Fix: return pathname\n\nNow let me capture the typecheck issue:\n- Root `npm run typecheck` fails \u2014 no workspace defines a `typecheck` script\n- Workaround: `npx tsc -p packages/<pkg>/tsconfig.json` per package\n- Root `tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.base.json` reports 68 errors (includes test files)\n- tsconfig.base.json: strict\n- Per-package tsconfig: `{ extends: \"../../tsconfig.base.json\", include: [\"src\"] }`\n\nEnvironment:\n- Repo: `/home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/metered-web-broker`\n- Packages: core, budget, audit, identity, rails, license, gateway\n- Namespace: `@mwb/*`\n- Node: v20.20.2 active; nvm has v22.22.1 and v20.20.0\n- tsc: 5.9.3\n- vitest: 2.1.9\n\nThread: `/home/iconbaypark2900/OpenWorker/knowledge/threads/metered-web-broker-repo-gate.md`\n\nTodos:\n1. Fix crypto fromJwk in identity/ring.ts (5 sites) \u2014 in_progress\n2. Fix budget engine ceiling semantics if a test requires it \u2014 pending\n3. Fix dashboard.ts ''-'' join bug \u2014 pending\n4. Fix policy.ts globMatch (cut off, but from previous summary it''s \"Fix policy.ts gl...\" which is \"globMatch\") \u2014 pending\nPlus the 4th was \"Phase 0 conformance harness package\" in the previous summary, but in the new content the 4th todo is cut off too. Let me reconstruct.\n\nFrom the new content, the todo_write shows 4 todos, the 4th is cut off: `{\"", "working_state": "## Working state (extracted mechanically from tool records)\nRecent shell commands:\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/metered-web-broker && npx vitest run 2>&1 | tail -60  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbayp