e restore the 58 lost points from memory.\"\n\nActually there''s a contradiction in the assistant''s own reasoning \u2014 \"keep the running record I should restore them from source-of-truth markdown\" vs \"I will not fabricate restore the 58 lost points from memory (that would violate the ''store only what you read, never infer'' rule)\". The resolution: verbatim text doesn''t exist for 08-26 points, so can''t restore them; the job is to ingest 08-27.\n\nHmm, actually \u2014 for the 08-26 source files, the assistant planned to read them to \"restore those 25 points verbatim.\" But then the final decision was to only ingest 08-27. Actually wait, the task says \"ingest yesterday''s findings.\" Today is 08-27. Yesterday would be 08-26. But the assistant read 08-27 files as \"today''s genuinely new daily outputs.\"\n\nLet me reconsider. The task says \"Take what the other automations wrote in the last 24 hours.\" The find command was `-mtime -1` (24 hours). The assistant determined the genuinely new files were the 08-27 ones (generated this morning), and the 08-26 files were \"touched by the scheduler.\" So the new findings to ingest are from the 08-27 files.\n\nSo the ingest target: 08-27 files (papers, breakage, jobs, repo-activity, morning-briefing, grants?). Plus maybe 08-26 market-brief and outside-view which weren''t in prior ledger.\n\nLet me note the files found:\n- /home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-tasks/__task__task-e6e7dcad9a/market-brief-2026-08-26.md\n- /home/iconbaypark2900/OpenWorker/__task__task-c685e22a0b/morning-briefing-2026-08-27.md (this was the most recent, 05:22 Aug 27)\n- /home/iconbaypark2900/OpenWorker/__task__task-1b2c4d3f13/papers-2026-08-27.md\n- /home/iconbaypark2900/OpenWorker/__task__task-f471043f3e/breakage-2026-08-27.md\n- /home/iconbaypark2900/OpenWorker/__task__task-c6cf366b90/jobs-2026-08-27.md\n- /home/iconbaypark2900/OpenWorker/__task__task-717e4360ea/repo-activity-2026-08-27.md\n- /home/iconbaypark2900/OpenWorker/__task__task-092a