body=None): data = json.dumps(body).encode() if body is not None else None req   [ok]\n- echo \"=== any ingest_kb.json anywhere ===\"; find /home/iconbaypark2900 -name ''ingest_kb.json'' -maxdepth 5 2>/dev/null | head; echo \"=== grep for 08-26 stored su  [ok]\n- echo \"=== state/scratch ingest_kb.json (date + count) ===\"; head -5 /home/iconbaypark2900/openworker/state/scratch/__task__task-ecad448aa3/ingest_kb.json; echo   [ok]\n- ls -la /home/iconbaypark2900/OpenWorker/__task__task-c685e22a0b/ | grep -E \"2026-08-2\" ; echo \"=== 08-26 source files present ===\"; for f in jobs-2026-08-26.md   [ok]\nTools used in the summarized span: brain_recall, list_files, memory_update, read_file, run_shell, todo_write, write_file", "user_messages": ["\u23f0 Scheduled run \u2014 Knowledge base \u2014 ingest yesterday''s findings This automation is due now: carry out the task below immediately and produce the result. The schedule already exists \u2014 do not create or modify any scheduled tasks. Take what the other automations wrote in the last 24 hours and put the findings into the Qdrant knowledge base, so later jobs (and I) can retrieve them by meaning instead of by remembering which file they were in. FIND the new outputs: `find /home/iconbaypark2900 -maxdepth 3 -path ''*__task__*'' -name ''*.md'' -mtime -1 | head -25` (task workspaces live under both ~/OpenWor\u2026"], "user_messages_dropped": 0, "created_at": 1787827726.2629528, "model_used": "openai:ornith-1.5-35b", "trimmed": false}');
