tasks workspace).\n\n10. The assistant wrote verify_agpack_tests.md in the workspace with the full report.\n\n11. The assistant counted and reconciled: 29+29+24 + 30+25+28+25 + 13 = 203. The stale \"10 failed / 72 passed\" was wrong.\n\n12. The user asked \"What is next to do?\"\n\n13. The assistant read validator.py, grepped for yaml/pyyaml/pydantic in .toml files, listed files.\n\n14. The assistant confirmed the production change (import pydantic + import yaml) was already applied in validator.py.\n\n15. The assistant checked pyproject.toml and _verify_all.py.\n\n16. The assistant identified the real next step: declare pydantic and PyYAML as runtime deps in pyproject.toml.\n\n17. The user responded \"Done. Both parts verified.\" \u2014 the manifest was fixed, and a clean pytest run showed 203 passed.\n\n18. The assistant did brain_note recording the fix, updated the thread, and confirmed verification complete.\n\n19. The user asked \"what is next to do?\" again.\n\n20. The assistant re-read the next-steps prompts: agpack-prompt-next.md, agpack-prompt-step3.md, metered-web-broker-next-steps-prompt.md.\n\nNow let me identify the key facts and constraints.\n\n**Project context:** agpack is a portable, verifiable agent runtime at `/home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/agpack`. It has a sandbox and a trust layer. The trust layer is \"Step 3.\"\n\n**Trust layer modules (Step 3):**\n- `trust/audit.py` \u2014 append-only replayable execution ledger (accountability half)\n- `trust/signing.py` \u2014 Ed25519 signature guarantee (cryptographic half)\n- `trust/delegation.py` \u2014 per-hop scoped tokens (authority half)\n\n**Test counts:**\n- test_trust_audit.py = 29\n- test_trust_delegation.py = 29\n- test_trust_signing.py = 24\n- test_sandbox_limits.py = 30\n- test_sandbox_host.py = 25\n- test_sandbox_imports.py = 28\n- test_sandbox_capabilities.py = 25\n- test_artifact_bundle.py = 13\n- Total = 203\n\n**Sandbox modules (Step 2, \"complete\"):**\n- capabilities.py \u2014 POLICY