n\nThe user hasn''t chosen. So the immediate next step is for the user to decide which thread to move.\n\nActually, let me reconsider. The user asked \"what is next to do?\" twice. The first time, the assistant gave the pyproject deps fix + pytest run, which the user did. The second time, the assistant re-read the next-steps prompts and offered options. The user''s last message is \"what is next to do?\" and the assistant responded with the options but no choice was made.\n\nSo the current state: verification is complete, the deps are declared, pytest is 203 passed. The next step is undecided \u2014 the user needs to pick a work stream.\n\nLet me also note the outstanding offer: \"a fresh-virtualenv pip install . + re-run to prove a clean install.\" The assistant offered this but it''s not clearly been requested.\n\nLet me now think about what I should capture for the \"pending tasks\":\n- Optional: fresh venv pip install . + re-run (offered, not confirmed)\n- Decision needed: which work stream to move into (agpack continuation vs metered-web-broker vs drug-discovery)\n- The metered-web-broker: \"Prove it before writing code. The repo is read-only \u2014 you cannot run npm inside it.\"\n\nLet me structure the summary.\n\nNow, one thing to verify: the count breakdown. Let me recheck:\n- trust_audit = 29\n- trust_delegation = 29\n- trust_signing = 24\n- sandbox_limits = 30 (22 non-parametrized + 3 parametrized \u00d7 3) \u2014 wait, 22 + 3\u00d73 = 22+9 = 31, but they wrote 30. Let me re-read: \"test_sandbox_limits.py = 30 (22 non-parametrized + 3 parametrized \u00d7 3)\". Hmm 22+9=31. But the total said 30. Actually the assistant wrote \"22 non-parametrized + 3 parametrized \u00d7 3\" but then 29+29+24 + 30+25+28+25 + 13. Let me just use 30 as the reported number. Actually there''s a discrepancy in my note, but the reported count for test_sandbox_limits.py is 30. I''ll note 30.\n\nActually, let me recompute the total: 29+29+24 = 82. 30+25+28+25 = 108. 82+108+13 = 203