nction correctly.\n\n5. Confirmed all three modules work via smoke tests.\n\n6. Updated todos \u2014 all 6 done:\n   - Write Phase notes file\n   - Implement audit.py\n   - Implement signing.py\n   - Implement delegation.py\n   - (presumably write tests)\n   - (presumably run tests)\n\n7. Listed files:\n   - `src/agpack/trust/`: `__init__.py`, `_phase3.md`, `audit.py`, `delegation.py`, `signing.py`\n   - `tests/`: `__init__.py`, `test_artifact_bundle.py`, `test_sandbox_capabilities.py`, `test_sandbox_host.py`, `test_sandbox_imports.py`, `test_sandbox_limits.py`\n\n8. No test file for trust modules existed yet.\n\n9. Read phase file `_phase3.md`.\n\n10. Confirmed `cryptography` is NOT a dependency (commented out), added it to pyproject.toml dependencies.\n\n11. Confirmed `schema.py` uses pydantic (already used), pydantic 2.13.4 installed.\n\n12. Wrote `tests/test_trust_signing.py`.\n\n13. Wrote `tests/test_trust_delegation.py` \u2014 had to rewrite the whole file because disk content didn''t match intended content (there was some broken/verbose helper code, and the file ended up at 391 lines).\n\nLet me look more carefully at the delegation.py details. The file is 483-486 lines. Key elements:\n- `ChainHop` dataclass with fields `sig`, and references to `iss`, `sub`, `scope`, `resource`, `budget`, `expires`, `max_scopes`, `capabilities`\n- `MAX_SCOPES = 1`\n- `SCHEME_ED25519 = \"ed25519\"`\n- `_scope_in_closed_set(scope)` \u2014 validates scope is in closed set\n- `_hop_canonical` \u2014 used in smoke test import\n- `_validate_resource`\n- `_namespace_of`\n- 8-step verify (from previous summary)\n\nFrom the tests written:\n- `ChainHop` has `sig` field\n- Functions: `verify`, `DelegationViolation`, `_hop_canonical`, `_base_sub_hop`, `_valid_token`, `_base_root_hop`\n- `token_id` matching for chain line tail\n- Test helpers: `_KEYS`, `_NOW`\n\nLet me extract the public API for tests. From delegation test:\n- `verify(tok, logical_now_unix=_NOW, keys=_KEYS)` \n- `DelegationViolation`\n- `_hop_canonical` imported\n\nNow, the key question: what is the CURRENT WORK state?\n\nThe very last action was:\n```\n[assistant \u2192 write_file] {\"path\": \"tests/test_trust_delegation.py\", \"content\": \"...\"}\n[tool result] tests/test_trust_delegation.py\n```\n\nAnd there was a `[dcode-proxy: the model spent its entire token budget reasoning and never emitted an answer.]` note at the top.\n\nSo the current work is: the assistant just finished writing `tests/test_trust_delegation.py`. It also wrote `tests/test_trust_signing.py`. It was mid-way through writing test files. Presumably it needs to write `tests/test_trust_audit.py` next, then run all tests.\n\nWait, let me re-read. The assistant wrote:\n- `tests/test_trust_signing.py` (complete, 391 lines? No wait)\n- `tests/test_trust_delegation.py`\n\nActually let me re-check. In the conversation:\n- First `write_file` for `tests/test_trust_signing.py` \u2014 content shown\n- Then `write_file` for `tests/test_trust_delegation.py` \u2014 content shown but then \"The disk file doesn''t match what I intended \u2014 it''s a different (broken) version. Let me just rewrite the entire file cleanly\"\n- Then another `write_file` for `tests/test_trust_delegation.py`\n\nSo `tests/test_trust_signing.py` is done, and `tests/test_trust_delegation.py` was just rewritten cleanly (last action).\n\nThe `test_trust_delegation.py` ended up 391 lines based on the read_file showing total_lines: 391. Wait, but that read happened BEFORE the final rewrite. Let me re-check the order:\n\n1. `[assistant \u2192 write_file] tests/test_trust_delegation.py` (first attempt)\n2. `[assistant \u2192 replace_in_file]` \u2014 \"I left some broken/verbose helper code... Let me clean up\" \u2014 ERROR: \"Expected 1 replacement(s), found 0\"\n3. `[assistant \u2192 read_file]` start_line 255 max 25 \u2014 shows 391 total lines\n4. `[assistant \u2192 write_file] tests/test_trust_delegation.py` \u2014 \"The disk file doesn''t match what I intended... Let me just rewrite the entire file cleanly\"\n\nSo the file was 391 lines, then rewritten. The final write_file is the last action.\n\nSo the current state:\n- All 3 modules implemented and smoke-tested\n- `tests/test_trust_signing.py` written\n- `tests/test_trust_delegation.py` just rewritten\n- Still need: `tests/test_trust_audit.py` (probably), then run all 3 test files with pytest\n\nLet me now figure out the public APIs from what''s been read, to include in artifacts/decisions.\n\n**signing.py** (230 lines):\n- `SCHEME_ED25519 = \"ed25519\"`\n- `_KEY_LEN = 32`\n- `_PUB_KEY_LEN = 32`\n- `canonical_manifest_bytes(manifest: Any) -> bytes` \u2014 THE shared function between packager and validator. Returns canonical bytes with `sign` cleared to null.\n- Functions: `sign`, `verify`, probably `SignatureBlock`, `SignatureVerificationError`\n- From previous summary: `verify(msg, sig)` returns bool, raises `SignatureVerificationError`\n\n**audit.py** (441 lines):\n- `AuditRecord` class with `ordinal` field (0-based position fixed forever once in ledger)\n- `ts_unix` field \u2014 logical time from `clock.now` scope\n- `replay(ledger, kind=None, ordinal_range=None, *, strict=True) -> list[dict]` \u2014 returns structured view\n- Functions: `AuditLedger` class, append, `LedgerCorrupt`\n- From previous summary: `AuditRecord`, `AuditLedger`, `replay`, `LedgerCorrupt`\n\n**delegation.py** (483-486 lines):\n- `ChainHop` dataclass (frozen) with `sig` field\n- `DelegationToken`\n- `verify`, `DelegationViolation`\n- `_hop_canonical`\n- `MAX_SCOPES = 1`\n- `SCHEME_ED25519 = \"ed25519\"`\n- `Scope` and `Budget` from `agpack.sandbox.capabilities` and `agpack.sandbox.limits`\n- 8-step verify: valid, expired, budget-widen, wrong-key all fail as intended\n\n**pyproject.toml**:\n- name = \"agpack\", version = \"0.0.0\"\n- Added `cryptography>=42` to dependencies\n- pydantic 2.13.4 already available (schema.py uses it)\n\n**Key decisions/errors:**\n1. Import convention: `fr