ally, it''s an error/issue note. But it''s about the proxy layer, not the agpack work. I''ll skip it as it''s not relevant to the task continuation \u2014 or I could note it. Given the instruction to \"preserve everything load-bearing,\" and this is about the session budget, it''s arguably not load-bearing for the agpack task. I''ll omit it to keep focus, or mention it minimally. I''ll omit it since it''s infra noise.\n\nLet me also reconsider the test file line counts. The signing test \u2014 I don''t have a read of it, so I don''t know its line count. The delegation test was 391 lines (before final rewrite) and then rewritten. The final rewrite content wasn''t shown in full.\n\nNow let me write concrete, load-bearing content.\n\nLet me structure:\n\n1. Primary request and intent\n2. Key concepts and decisions\n3. Artifacts and files\n4. Errors and fixes\n5. All user messages\n6. Pending tasks\n7. Current work\n8. Next step\n\nFor user messages \u2014 in this conversation, there are NO explicit user messages visible. The \"[assistant \u2192 ...]\" and \"[tool result]\" are all assistant/tool actions. There''s no user text. The only \"user\" content is the system instruction at the very top asking to produce the summary. So the \"All user messages\" section would note there were no substantive user messages in this segment. That''s an important audit note.\n\nLet me write it.\n\nFor the public API, let me be careful to only state what''s confirmed. Let me note the confirmed APIs from imports that were actually executed successfully in smoke tests:\n- `from agpack.trust.signing import ...` \u2014 worked\n- `from agpack.trust.delegation import DelegationToken, ChainHop, verify, DelegationViolation, _hop_canonical` \u2014 worked\n- `from agpack.trust.audit import ...` \u2014 worked (in earlier, PYTHONPATH=src)\n\nLet me write the summary.\n\nActually, for the delegation.py public API, let me extract more carefully. From the read_file output and tests:\n- `ChainHop` \u2