oot_is_root = line 226\n- test_chain_line_tail_must_be_sub = line 239\n- test_chain_line_no_cycles = line 254\n- test_hop_signature_wrong_key_rejected = line 272\n- test_policy_type_available = line 363\n\nSo these 6 are the named tests. The diagnosis said \"5 delegation tests fail\" \u2014 so 5 of these 6 fail, 1 passes. Which one passes? Probably test_policy_type_available passes (it expects TypeError from CapabilityPolicy(scope=...), which IS raised). And the other 5 fail.\n\nActually, the assistant''s earlier note said \"test_policy_type_available ... would raise TypeError \u2014 which is actually what the test name suggests. But the summary flagged it as a failure.\" So the summary listed it as failing, but on fresh inspection, the test might already pass. So it''s one of the 5 that fails vs 6th that passes.\n\nHmm, but actually the summary said 8 failures: 2 audit + 6 delegation. The 6 delegation were: test_scope_closed_rejects_unrecognised, test_chain_line_single_hop_root_is_root, test_chain_line_tail_must_be_sub, test_chain_line_no_cycles, test_hop_signature_wrong_key_rejected, test", "working_state": "## Working state (extracted mechanically from tool records)\nRecent shell commands:\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/agpack && echo \"--- AuditRecord( usages ---\" && grep -rn \"AuditRecord(\" src tests | head -n 30 && echo \"--- _detail_ok usag  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/agpack && echo \"=== delegation.py defs ===\" && grep -n \"^def \\|^class \\|def verify\\|def __\" src/agpack/trust/delegation.py   [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/agpack && python -m pytest tests/test_trust_delegation.py tests/test_trust_audit.py -q 2>&1 | tail -n 40  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/agpack && python -m pytest tests/test_trust_delegation.py::test_scope_closed_rejects_unrecognised tests/test_trust_delegati  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/agpack && echo \"=== asserts on old audit msg ===\" && grep -rn \"missing/incorrect required field\\|detail is corrupt\" tests &  [exit 1]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/agpack && echo \"=== _record and _ledger_from ===\" && sed -n ''61,100p'' tests/test_trust_audit.py  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/agpack && echo \"=== _detail_ok usages ===\" && grep -rn \"_detail_ok\\|_detail_bad\" src tests && echo \"=== trust/ dir ===\" &&   [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/agpack && grep -n \"_detail_ok\\|_detail_bad\\|corrupt\" src/agpack/trust/audit.py  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/agpack && python -m pytest tests/test_trust_audit.py -q 2>&1 | tail -n 15  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/agpack && grep -n \"_RESOURCE_MIN_LABELS\\|_NSPACES\\|_PREFIX\\|_NAME_RE\" src/agpack/trust/delegation.py | head  [ok]\nTools used in the summarized span: grep, read_file, replace_in_file, run_shell, todo_write", "user_messages": ["Reproduce the suite \u2014 copy agpack into a writable scratch dir, install deps, run pytest on all three test_trust_*.py, and save the real output. No green claims without this. Branch A \u2014 something''s broken \u2192 fix it (the prompt flags the specific suspect): test_trust_signing.test_canonical_manifest_bytes_is_stable builds an AgentBundleManifest with components missing the required cid/kind/file fields, which should raise a pydantic error \u2014 so that test likely errors, not passes. Instruction: fix the test to construct a valid manifest, don''t weaken the schema to paper over a bad test. Branch B \u2014 i\u2026", "Branch A into the audit + delegation suites"], "user_messages_dropped": 0, "created_at": 1787954206.1137183, "model_used": "openai:ornith-1.5-35b", "trimmed": false}');
