g, grep handleFetch\n10. Read vitest.config.ts, gateway/tsconfig.json\n11. Read tsconfig.base.json, budget/src/engine.ts\n12. todo_write update\n13. replace_in_file on types.ts \u2014 adding finality field to FetchOutcome\n14. replace_in_file on broker.ts \u2014 finality builder gated on reconcile().ok\n15. replace_in_file on broker.ts \u2014 import AuditLedger\n16. replace_in_file on broker.ts \u2014 import { AuditLedger, reconcile }\n17. todo_write update\n18. write_file packages/gateway/src/metered-origin.test.ts\n19. read_file metered-origin.test.ts (re-read to confirm)\n\nKey facts established:\n- User said \"not in plan mode \u2014 proceed with the work directly\" \u2014 so the assistant should NOT use propose_plan/plan mode. Work directly.\n- The `finality` flag was added to FetchOutcome in types.ts (line after completedAt/error)\n- The `reconcile` import was added to broker.ts\n- The broker.fulfilled builder now sets finality, gated on reconcile().ok\n- P2 is done (2 tasks)\n- P1 test file being created at packages/gateway/src/metered-origin.test.ts\n\nLet me think about the actual technical decisions:\n\n**P2 \u2014 finality flag:**\n- Added `finality?: ''claimed'' | ''final''` to FetchOutcome in types.ts (based on the replacement \u2014 the old string was `tenantId?: string; timestamps: { startedAt: string; completedAt: string }; error?: { code: string; message: string };}` and new adds finality)\n- In broker.ts, `fulfilled()` builder now sets finality gated on reconcile().ok\n- The comment: \"Finality: only when the ledger as a whole reconciles clean is the fulfillment *finally* settled \u2014 not merely the o[urcome]...\"\n\n**P1 \u2014 test file metered-origin.test.ts:**\n- Real metered origin with Ed25519 verification\n- Round trip: 402 (proof missing) \u2192 settle \u2192 200 (proof present) \u2192 402 on replay\n- Plus origin refusing bad/replayed proofs\n\nLet me think about the module resolution finding:\n- vitest config: `include: [''packages/*/src/**/*.test.ts'']`, environment: node\n- tsconfig.base.json: moduleResolution: Bundler, module: ESNext\n- `.js` extension aliases to `.ts` \u2014 so `./server.js` resolves in tests\n\nImportant constraint note from user message at the very start:\n\"[previous compaction summary...]\"\n\"[dcode-proxy: the model spent its entire token budget reasoning and never emitted an answer. Its reasoning is shown below. Raise max_tokens to get a real answer.]\"\n\nThis is a system/proxy note. The actual conversation then begins with the previous compaction summary content, then \"[conversation since]\".\n\nWait, let me re-read. The structure is:\n- \"[previous compaction summary \u2014 fold its still-relevant content into the new summary]\"\n- Then the previous compaction summary text (the dcode-proxy reasoning block)\n- \"[conversation since]\"\n- Then the actual new conversation\n\nSo the previous compaction summary is the big block of reasoning that was shown. And then \"conversation since\" has the actual new actions.\n\nLet me capture the errors and fixes:\n1. propose_plan rejected: \"not in plan mode \u2014 proceed with the work directly\" \u2014 user correction. Fix: proceeded directly, using todo_write and direct edits.\n2. The \"metered-web-broker-next-steps-prompt.md\" doesn''t exist \u2014 handled by proceeding with the 4 priorities from the message. (This was in the previous compaction, still relevant.)\n\nNow let me think about the current state at the end:\n- P2 source changes are done (finality in types.ts, finality set in broker.fulfilled gated on reconcile().ok)\n- The metered-origin.test.ts file was written (write_file tool result confirms path)\n- The last action was read_file metered-origin.test.ts (re-read)\n\nSo the current work is: the P1 test file just got written, then re-read. The next step would be to run the tests and typecheck.\n\nWait \u2014 let me check the todo list. The last todo_write showed:\n```\n{\"content\": \"P1+P2: real 402 -> settle -> 200 round trip through the broke\u2026\", \"status\": ...}\n```\nLet me look. The todo lists at the end:\n- First update: P2 add finality (in_progress), P2 set finality in broker.fulfilled (pending), P1+P2 test (pending), plus \"Re-read\" (done) \u2014 wait that was 4 shown but count was 5.\n- The 5th todo wasn''t shown (truncated). Actually the first todo_write returned count:5 with 4 shown. Let me reconstruct.\n\nActually there are two todo_write calls after source changes:\n1. After types.ts + broker.ts edits: count:5, shows 4 todos, content truncated at \"P2: set finality in broker.fulfilled, gated on reconcile().fi\u2026\"\n2. write_file: no todo shown in result.\n3. read_file metered-origin.test.ts: no todo.\n\nHmm wait, let me re-read. The sequence:\n\n```\n[assistant \u2192 todo_write] {todos with 4 shown: \"Re-read done\", \"P2 add finality\", \"P2 set finality in broker.fulfilled gated on reconcile().fi\", \"P1+P2 real 402 -> settle -> 200 round trip through the broke\u2026\"}\n```\nThat''s the one before replace_in_file on types.ts. Then:\n\n```\n[assistant \u2192 replace_in_file] types.ts (finality field)\n[assistant \u2192 replace_in_file] broker.ts (finality builder)\n[assistant \u2192 replace_in_file] broker.ts (import AuditLedger)\n[assistant \u2192 replace_in_file] broker.ts (import reconcile)\n[assistant \u2192 todo_write] {todos: 5, shows 4: \"Re-read done\", \"P2 add finality\", \"P2 set finality\", \"P1+P2 round trip...\"}\n[assistant \u2192 write_file] metered-origin.test.ts\n[assistant] \"Re-read complete. Final detail confirmed...\"\n[assistant \u2192 read_file] metered-origin.test.ts\n```\n\nSo after the source edits and second todo update, the write_file created metered-origin.test.ts. Then re-read it.\n\nThe 5th todo (hidden) \u2014 probably something like \"Typecheck + run all tests to confirm P1+P2\". Since the first todo had 5 and only 4 shown. Let me reconstruct the 5th: given \"Re-read done\" (1), \"P2 add finality\" (2), \"P2 set finality in broker.fulfilled\" (3), \"P1+P2 round trip test\" (4), the 5th was likely \"Run typecheck + tests to verify\" or \"update build-plan/talking-points\". Given the discipline (\"read-only verification discipline\" \u2014 verify by reading, not mutating), the 5th was probably \"run vitest to verify the round trip passes\".\n\nActually, I shouldn''t over-speculate about the 5th todo. Let me note it as \"likely a verify/tests todo, hidden in truncation.\"\n\nNow, at the very end, the re-read of metered-origin.test.ts was to \"confirm... module resolution is Bundler with .js extension aliases to .ts, so ./server.js resolves in tests.\" So the assistant re-read the file after writing it to confirm it''s correct.\n\nThe next step: run the tests (vitest) and typecheck to verify the P1 round-trip test passes and P2 finality works. This aligns with the \"read-only verification discipline\" and the pending verify todo.\n\nLet me now think about what''s load-bearing to preserve:\n\n**Files modified (load-bearing):**\n1. packages/core/src/types.ts \u2014 added `finality?: ''claimed'' | ''final''` to FetchOutcome (and possibly related types). The replacement shows: old ended with `tenantId?: string; timestamps: { startedAt: string; completedAt: string }; error?: { code: string; message: string };}`, new was `tenantId?: stri\u2026` (truncated). chars_before: 4265, chars_after: 4600, so +335 chars. This added the finality field and probably a doc comment.\n2. packages/gateway/src/broker.ts \u2014 added reconcile import, and set finality in fulfilled() gated on reconcile().ok. 3 replacements.\n3. packages/gateway/src/metered-origin.test.ts \u2014 NEW test file, P1+P2 round trip.\n\n**Key technical decisions:**\n- P2: `finality` flag added to FetchOutcome. Only when reconcile().ok === true is fulfillment \"finally\" settled (not merely claimed). This prevents \"betting real settlement on an assumption\" about origin 2xx.\n- Broker settles BEFORE origin.fetch (per selfsettle.ts docstring). So a real self-402 fetch presents a signed mandate to the metered origin \u2192 origin releases content.\n- Reconcile in audit ledger is the source of truth for finality.\n- P1 test uses REAL SelfHosted402Rail + REAL metered origin with Ed25519 verification \u2014 no stubs/dummies.\n\n**Verification discipline constraint:** The user wants work verified by reading/testing, not by mutating production. Actually the \"read-only verification discipline\" from the previous summary means: verify by reading (tests, typecheck) rather than mutating live/main. And \"scratch/staging\" \u2014 work in scratch/staging. This is a standing constraint. Let me preserve it but not overstate. Actually I should be careful \u2014 the previous summary wasn''t 100% sure what this meant. I''ll note it as stated by the user in the prior summary with the caveat that the exact meaning was still being interpreted. Actually the previous compaction said: \"verify by reading, not by mutating? Hmm, ''read-only verification discipline.''\" Let me just record it as a stated standing constraint and note it needs interpretation.\n\nHmm, actually let me reconsider. Is this really a standing constraint? The previous compaction was uncertain. But it''s the best info I have. I''ll record it as \"stated standing constraint (per prior context), interpretation: work in scratch/staging, verify via read-only checks/tests rather than mutating production/main.\" I''ll flag that its precise scope may need confirmation. Actually, to avoid relitigation but preserve load-bearing info, I''ll record it plainly and note the interpretation.\n\nLet me think about whether I need to flag it as needing confirmation. The rule says \"Constraints outlive the turns they were stated in.\" So I should preserve it. But the previous compaction flagged uncertainty. I''ll record it as stated but note the interpretation is the assistant''s reading.\n\n**User messages:**\nThe only NEW user message in \"conversation since\" is:\n- `{\"approved\": false, \"error\": \"not in plan mode \u2014 proceed with the work directly\"}` \u2014 this is the plan-mode rejection.\n\nWait, is that a \"user message\"? It''s a tool result from a plan-mode check. The instructions say \"a chronological list of every user message.\" This is a user/system correction. I''ll include it as a user message (it''s a user directive).\n\nActually the previous compaction summary captured the user''s two messages:\n1. The big next-steps prompt message (P1-P4 priorities).\n2. The answers JSON (3 clarifying questions).\n\nThese are from before the compaction. Since the previous summary is being folded in, I should include those too in the \"All user messages\" section? The instruction says \"fold its still-relevant content into the new summary.\" The \"All user messages\" section is part of the new summary. The prior summary listed those messages. Since they''re the origin of the priorities and scope, they''re still relevant/needed for the audit trail. I''ll include them but note they''re from the prior context.", "working_state": "## Working state (extracted mechanically from tool records)\nFiles written/edited (most recent first):\n- packages/gateway/src/metered-origin.test.ts\nRecent shell commands:\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/metered-web-broker; echo ''=== vitest config ===''; ls vitest.config.* vite.config.* 2>/dev/null; echo ''--- root tsconfig ---  [exit 1]\nTools used in the summarized span: propose_plan, read_file, replace_in_file, run_shell, todo_write, write_file", "user_messages": ["Next-steps prompt: metered-web-broker-next-steps-prompt.md Four priorities, sequenced so the load-bearing work comes first: P1 \u2014 wire ONE real 402 \u2192 settle \u2192 200 round-trip. The bearing thesis. Verify a real metered origin (don''t assume x402 names), read the PaymentRail seam, implement a spec-agnostic rail, add replay/nonce guards, and prove the loop on real bytes. P2 \u2014 add the finality flag, in the same pass. test/claimed \u2192 conditional outcome; only reconcile().ok === true \u2192 true fulfilled. Closes the \"don''t bet real settlement on an assumption\" move. P3 \u2014 upgrade conformance to Tier B. Live\u2026"], "user_messages_dropped": 0, "created_at": 1787958258.2686577, "model_used": "openai:ornith-1.5-35b", "trimmed": false}');
INSERT INTO sessions VALUES('0337e3fa-add','/home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/agpack','openai:ornith-1.5-35b','auto','Branch B — it''s green → next step is Step 4, Portability. If','builder',346,NULL,'[]',0,0,NULL,NULL,'Agpack Portability Build',0,'2026-08-28 23:24:09','{}','{"boundary_index": 312, "summary_text": "## 1. Primary request and intent\n\n- **Goal:** Implement the `src/agpack/portability/` modules (`driver.py`, `profiles.py`, `compat_harness.py`) as **concrete, working wasmtime-based drivers** that integrate end-to-end with the agpack sandbox host \u2014 completing \"step 4\" (portability) of the project.\n- **Context:** agpack is a WASM-based secure-tool sandbox for agent tool calls. Project root: `/home/iconbaypark2900/dataScience/agpack`.\n- **Host contract (driver-agnostic):** host hands driver `(module_bytes, imports, budget, audit)` and asks for a `RunResult`-shaped outcome. Driver lifecycle is `name` / `instantiate` / `dispose`; an `Instance` exposes `call` / `peak_memory_pages`.\n- **Standing constraint (from prior turn):** \"never send without my approval\" \u2014 see \u00a76; **flagged as UNCERTAIN/UNCONFIRMED** (no human turn has occurred since; treat as unverified until the user restates it).\n\n## 2. Key concepts and decisions\n\n- **Validated wasmtime API** (proven in `.scratch/probe_bind.py`, end-to-end):\n  - `import wasmtime as w`; `w.Config()` \u2192 `w.Engine(cfg)` \u2192 `w.Store(eng)` \u2192 `w.Module(eng, bytearray(w.wat2wasm(WAT)))`.\n  - `w.ValType.i32()` is a **factory method \u2014 call with parens** (not attribute access).\n  - `w.FuncType(inputs, outputs)`, e.g. `w.FuncType([], [w.ValType.i32()])`, `w.FuncType([w.ValType.i32(), w.ValType.i32()], [w.ValType.i32()])`.\n  - Host funcs: `w.Func(st, ty, fn, access_caller=True)` \u2014 fn receives a `caller`.\n  - **WAT ordering: imports must precede memory** in the module.\n  - Instantiation: single `w.Instance(st, mod, [])`; then re-fetch `ex = inst.exports(st)` (memory is re-created/grown between calls, so cached memory objects go stale).\n  - Call: `rp, rl = ex[\"run\"](st, 0, len(args))` \u2192 returns tuple.\n  - Memory: `mem.write(st, value, start)` (arg order = **st, value, start**); `mem.read(st, start, length)`; `mem.size(st)` \u2192 pages; `mem.data_len(st)` \u2192 bytes; `mem.grow(st, n)` \u2192 next page count or `-1` on failure.\n  - `Caller` exposes only `.get(name)`; `caller.get(\"mem\")` returns exported memory; `cmem.read(caller, ptr, length)`.\n  - Fuel: `st.set_fuel(n)` / `st.get_fuel()`; exhaustion \u2192 `w.Trap`.\n  - WAT compile: `w.wat2wasm(WAT)` compiles.\n- **`build_imports` contract (NEW insight this turn):** returns `dict[str, Callable]`; each fn takes **native** args (str/bytes), but the **guest calls with pointer+len i32s via memory** \u2192 **the driver must translate** guest ptr/len calls \u2192 native fn args.\n- **Host contract types** (from `host.py`/`limits.py`/`capabilities.py`/`imports.py`):\n  - `Budget(fuel_max, memory_pages_max, wall_time_ms)` \u2014 3 required args.\n  - `CapabilityPolicy(scopes, params)`: `scopes: frozenset[Scope] = frozenset()`, `params: dict[Scope, CapabilityParams] = factory`. Methods: `includes(scope)`, `as_scopes()`, `param(scope)`.\n  - `Scope` values render as `agpack/<name>`; look up via `Scope.from_raw_name(...)` (see `capabilities.py`).\n  - `LimitError` subclasses: `FuelExhausted(msg, spent)`, `MemoryExhausted(msg, spent)`, `Timeout(spent, budget, fuel_meter_bug_suspect=)`.\n- **`import_call`/fuel records** are appended by `build_imports` \u2014 driver consumes those import names.\n- **wasmer status:** `import wasmer` fails (`Wasmer is not available on this system`); pip shows only `wasmer` 1.1.0 max. `WasmerDriver` in `profiles.py` **must degrade gracefully with no hard `import wasmer`**.\n\n## 3. Artifacts and files\n\n- **`src/agpack/portability/driver.py`** (85 lines) \u2014 **STILL A STUB**. The load-bearing `RuntimeDriver` interface. Docstring: \"The host is *driver-agnostic*: it hands the driver `(module_bytes, imports, budget, audit)` and asks for a `RunResult`-shaped outcome. A driv\u2026\" \u2192 **targets implementation.**\n- **`src/agpack/portability/profiles.py`** (90 lines) \u2014 **STILL A STUB**. Drivers + profile pluggability: \"a profile is a triple of `(driver, budget-normalization, tolerance-shape)`.\" \u2192 **targets implementation.**\n- **`src/agpack/portability/compat_harness.py`** (88 lines) \u2014 **STILL A STUB**. Step-4 demo: \"same bundle, two profiles, one verdict.\" \u2192 **targets implementation.**\n- **`src/agpack/artifact/schema.py`** (366 lines) \u2014 **read**; defines `BundleFileReader` shape the driver may rely on for reading bundle payloads.\n- **`src/agpack/sandbox/capabilities.py`** (359 lines) \u2014 **read**; `Scope`, `Scope.from_raw_name`, policy data model.\n- **`src/agpack/sandbox/imports.py`** (463 lines) \u2014 **read**; `build_imports` (returns `dict[str, Callable]`, native-arg fns) \u2014 the door the guest calls through.\n- **`src/agpack/sandbox/host.py`** (449 lines) \u2014 **read**; integration point that wires capabilities/limits/imports/engine.\n- **`src/agpack/sandbox/limits.py`** (337 lines) \u2014 **read (lines 1\u2013130)**; `Budget` + `LimitError` family; fuel is a monotonically-increasing per-run meter.\n- **`.scratch/probe_bind.py`** (55 lines) \u2014 **read**; validated reference probe (the working wasmtime round-trip). Its WAT: imports `agpack/emit.text` `(param i32 i32)`, `agpack/clock.now`, memory export `mem`, func export `run`.\n- `.scratch/probe_contract.py` (23 lines), `.scratch/wasm_probe.py` \u2014 still exist; not re-read this turn.\n\n## 4. Errors and fixes\n\n- `w.ValType.i32` as attribute \u2192 **it''s a factory: `w.ValType.i32()`**.\n- `w.Func(..., can_call_python=True)` invalid \u2192 correct kwarg is `access_caller=True` (confirmed via `inspect.signature(w.Func.__init__)`).\n- `out_mem.write(st, 0, args)` wrong order \u2192 correct is `write(st, value, start)`; used `write(st, args, 0)`.\n- Stale memory object after `run` \u2192 **re-fetch `ex[\"mem\"]`/`inst.exports(st)` after each call** (memory re-created/grown).\n- WAT string-concat errors \u2192 **imports must precede memory**; explicit `+` / well-formed paren batches in the `(module ...)` assembly.\n- `compile_ok()` called with wrong arg count \u2192 fixed to 2 args.\n-", "working_state": "## Working state (extracted mechanically from tool records)\nTools used in the summarized span: list_file_dirs, list_files, read_file", "user_messages": ["Branch B \u2014 it''s green \u2192 next step is Step 4, Portability. If the trust suite reproduces green, the README''s own build order says Step 4 (\"the same bundle executes unchanged on two different runtimes\") is next: build agpack/portability/ (driver.py, profiles.py wasmtime/wasmer, compat_harness.py) that runs one bundle across two drivers and diffs the RunResult \u2014 while freezing host.py and all trust modules."], "user_messages_dropped": 0, "created_at": 1787959299.9992442, "model_used": "openai:ornith-1.5-35b", "trimmed": false}');
